WEBVTT

1
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:47.250
<i>My name is Happy Gilmore.</i>

2
00:00:48.375 --> 00:00:51.625
<i>Growing up, I always
wanted to be a hockey player.</i>

3
00:00:51.708 --> 00:00:54.583
<i>But then 30 years ago,
I picked up a golf club.</i>

4
00:00:57.875 --> 00:00:59.833
<i>Turned out to be a pretty good decision.</i>

5
00:00:59.917 --> 00:01:03.833
<i>And Happy Gilmore wins the 98th U.S. Open.</i>

6
00:01:03.917 --> 00:01:06.958
<i>I got to marry
a great lady named Virginia,</i>

7
00:01:07.042 --> 00:01:08.958
<i>and we had a son named Gordy.</i>

8
00:01:09.708 --> 00:01:12.250
<i>The wins didn't always come as expected,</i>

9
00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:14.208
<i>but like Grandma always said,</i>

10
00:01:14.292 --> 00:01:17.250
<i>sometimes it's better
to be lucky than good.</i>

11
00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:20.625
Oh, Lord!

12
00:01:20.708 --> 00:01:22.542
I made it!

13
00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:26.250
<i>Yeah, I was getting lucky
in more ways than one.</i>

14
00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:28.333
He shoots, he scores!

15
00:01:28.417 --> 00:01:30.417
<i>And after our fourth boy in four years,</i>

16
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.250
<i>Virginia had an idea for an endorsement.</i>

17
00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:36.000
<i>Trojan. Kids are great…</i>

18
00:01:37.708 --> 00:01:39.250
<i>…in moderation.</i>

19
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:41.500
<i>What are you doing? Calm down!</i>

20
00:01:42.125 --> 00:01:45.083
<i>I tried to get the boys
into competitive golf tournaments…</i>

21
00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:48.333
Follow that.

22
00:01:48.417 --> 00:01:50.958
<i>But their hockey instincts
were too strong.</i>

23
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.292
Boys, stop! Come on, what are you doing?

24
00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:01.708
<i>Tiger Woods had a video game,
so we did a Happy Gilmore one.</i>

25
00:02:01.792 --> 00:02:05.042
<i>But I think the computer guys
made it a little too realistic.</i>

26
00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.167
<i>You've had enough.</i>

27
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.833
<i>Anyways, the boys loved
how violent it was,</i>

28
00:02:08.917 --> 00:02:11.125
<i>but it made my little girl nervous.</i>

29
00:02:11.208 --> 00:02:13.917
<i>That's right,
we finally had a little girl,</i>

30
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.167
<i>sweet Vienna, Mommy's new best friend.</i>

31
00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.542
<i>Oh, and I hosted </i>Saturday Night Live
<i>a few times. That was nice.</i>

32
00:02:20.625 --> 00:02:22.458
<i>The Spice Girls are here!</i>

33
00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.958
<i>Maroon 5 is here!</i>

34
00:02:24.042 --> 00:02:28.250
<i>The Weeknd is here!
So stick around, we'll be right back.</i>

35
00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:31.375
<i>Yeah, we had it all, so I told Virginia…</i>

36
00:02:31.458 --> 00:02:35.042
We should just retire
so we can hang out with the kids all day.

37
00:02:35.125 --> 00:02:36.750
We're not done with golf, Happy.

38
00:02:36.833 --> 00:02:38.250
And golf's not done with us.

39
00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:42.542
It's like Chubbs used to say.
We've only just begun.

40
00:02:42.625 --> 00:02:43.625
Hmm.

41
00:02:44.708 --> 00:02:45.792
Gordy!

42
00:02:45.875 --> 00:02:48.042
Oh, come on,
don't pee on the slip-n-slide.

43
00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:50.000
Appreciate your time today.
It's Mother's Day.

44
00:02:50.083 --> 00:02:52.083
We honor all of the mothers
who are watching.

45
00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.583
Let's go real deep now!

46
00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:57.625
<i>But in golf,
even when you're at the top of your game…</i>

47
00:02:57.708 --> 00:02:59.583
<i>You can always shank one.</i>

48
00:03:03.625 --> 00:03:04.625
Uh-oh.

49
00:03:06.708 --> 00:03:11.958
<i>After the funeral, I decided
I would never pick up a golf club again.</i>

50
00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:15.125
<i>I was now
a single father of five children.</i>

51
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.708
<i>There was really
only one thing I could do…</i>

52
00:03:19.583 --> 00:03:21.000
<i>I'd never been a big boozer,</i>

53
00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:23.292
<i>but alcohol was the only thing
that helped me</i>

54
00:03:23.375 --> 00:03:26.333
<i>to forget what I'd done
to the sweetest woman I'd ever known.</i>

55
00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:28.875
<i>- Oh, one more thing…</i>
- It's no good.

56
00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:30.875
<i>The money.</i>

57
00:03:30.958 --> 00:03:31.958
Give me the…

58
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.708
No, no, dude! Come on, man.

59
00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:38.792
<i>See, Virginia always handled the finances,</i>

60
00:03:38.875 --> 00:03:41.708
<i>so without her,
a lot of stuff fell through the cracks.</i>

61
00:03:41.792 --> 00:03:43.417
Should I smash the window?

62
00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.792
<i>Then I caught some guy
trying to break into my Ferrari.</i>

63
00:03:46.875 --> 00:03:48.625
Hey, can you hold my beer?

64
00:03:48.708 --> 00:03:50.250
Yeah.

65
00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:54.083
<i>The guy wasn't a thief, he was a repo man.</i>

66
00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.333
Can you let me explain?

67
00:03:55.417 --> 00:03:58.292
<i>Turns out I didn't know
I had to renew the lease.</i>

68
00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:01.208
<i>The big baby sued me,
and I lost everything…</i>

69
00:04:01.917 --> 00:04:04.708
<i>Including Grandma's house,
which was devastating.</i>

70
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.375
<i>The boys had to
move into an apartment together,</i>

71
00:04:20.458 --> 00:04:24.125
<i>and me and Vienna
found a new place that was affordable.</i>

72
00:04:26.417 --> 00:04:30.708
<i>It's not the best neighborhood,
but it's walkable to my new job.</i>

73
00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:34.917
<i>Gary, can you pick up in section 2?</i>

74
00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:48.167
Happy Gilmore.
Oh, my God, I'm such a massive fan.

75
00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.083
Okay, bro, what can I help you with?

76
00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:52.167
You ever hear of Maxi Sports Drink?

77
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.750
I think that's aisle four.

78
00:04:53.833 --> 00:04:55.917
No. It's my company, I own it.

79
00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.208
I'm Frank Manatee.

80
00:04:57.292 --> 00:05:00.417
My real passion is this cutting-edge
golf project that I've been working on.

81
00:05:01.583 --> 00:05:04.125
I don't golf no more, brother.

82
00:05:04.208 --> 00:05:05.542
Cucumber juice in there?

83
00:05:05.625 --> 00:05:07.000
Sure.

84
00:05:07.083 --> 00:05:09.167
Anyway, I figured
maybe you would start golfing again

85
00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.250
once you heard
how huge this league was gonna be.

86
00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:13.500
I wish you luck, but I'm not interested.

87
00:05:13.583 --> 00:05:16.167
See, that's the thing.
Nobody's interested in traditional golf.

88
00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.833
It's a boring sport
played by boring people.

89
00:05:18.917 --> 00:05:20.833
They ain't boring, they're my friends.

90
00:05:20.917 --> 00:05:23.458
You don't understand.
You inspired this thing, all right?

91
00:05:23.542 --> 00:05:25.750
And I love you,
and I'd hate to see you pass this up

92
00:05:25.833 --> 00:05:28.542
and have your life turn out
worse than it already is.

93
00:05:29.125 --> 00:05:31.375
I get it. Golf makes you tense, right?

94
00:05:31.458 --> 00:05:32.792
Because the whole wife thing?

95
00:05:32.875 --> 00:05:35.167
Get your skunk breath
out of my face, or I swear to God...

96
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.792
Or what, tough guy?
You're not gonna do a damn thing about it,

97
00:05:37.875 --> 00:05:41.458
because if you lay one finger on me,
you're going right to jail.

98
00:05:41.542 --> 00:05:43.167
That's if I get caught.

99
00:05:44.958 --> 00:05:45.958
<i>Operations.</i>

100
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.292
Hey, Linda, can you turn
the security cameras off for 90 seconds?

101
00:05:59.958 --> 00:06:05.625
Seven, eight. Fouetté, fouetté. Finish.

102
00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:10.208
Great. Arms, fifth. Soutenu.

103
00:06:11.542 --> 00:06:13.750
Fouetté, fouetté.

104
00:06:14.833 --> 00:06:16.625
Arms, fifth.

105
00:06:17.542 --> 00:06:21.750
Soutenu. Chaîné, chaîné.

106
00:06:21.833 --> 00:06:23.958
And arabesque.

107
00:06:25.417 --> 00:06:26.500
Look at that.

108
00:06:27.208 --> 00:06:28.250
Daddy!

109
00:06:28.333 --> 00:06:29.833
Hey, Vienna.

110
00:06:30.875 --> 00:06:34.667
Oh, with the kicks!
Hey. The Rockettes are here.

111
00:06:35.917 --> 00:06:37.250
Glad you're home.

112
00:06:37.333 --> 00:06:39.417
You were a clue on <i>Jeopardy!</i>
Let me show you.

113
00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.792
Really?

114
00:06:40.875 --> 00:06:42.542
Okay. Hi.

115
00:06:42.625 --> 00:06:43.542
Hi.

116
00:06:43.625 --> 00:06:45.250
How'd my girl do today?

117
00:06:45.333 --> 00:06:48.917
Great. Beyond great.
She needs a better teacher than me.

118
00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.083
- Look.
- Yeah.

119
00:06:50.167 --> 00:06:52.750
<i>With his amazing long drives
and hockey player's temper,</i>

120
00:06:52.833 --> 00:06:58.000
<i>this golfer won the first of his six
Tour Championships in 1996. Carter?</i>

121
00:06:58.083 --> 00:06:59.375
Who is Happy Goldberg?

122
00:06:59.458 --> 00:07:01.167
Sorry, no. Ling.

123
00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.875
Who is Happy Gudenstein?

124
00:07:02.958 --> 00:07:04.792
Nope. Jana.

125
00:07:04.875 --> 00:07:07.458
Who is Skippy Goldenbaum?

126
00:07:07.542 --> 00:07:09.292
That is incorrect.

127
00:07:09.375 --> 00:07:12.458
He is Jewish,
but we were looking for Happy Gilmore.

128
00:07:12.542 --> 00:07:13.875
At least he knew it.

129
00:07:13.958 --> 00:07:15.750
I'm making your grandma's
brisket for dinner.

130
00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:16.833
The boys are coming.

131
00:07:16.917 --> 00:07:18.833
Okay, good. Good, I can't wait.

132
00:07:19.542 --> 00:07:22.167
What do you mean, a better teacher?
Are you quitting?

133
00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.375
No, but I work at the Boys and Girls Club.

134
00:07:24.458 --> 00:07:26.667
She's light years
beyond anyone else I ever taught.

135
00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.542
So what? Where should she go?

136
00:07:28.625 --> 00:07:31.083
The Paris Opera Ballet School.

137
00:07:31.167 --> 00:07:33.042
Where's that? Around here?

138
00:07:33.125 --> 00:07:35.208
It's in Paris.

139
00:07:35.958 --> 00:07:38.083
They only have four slots open each year.

140
00:07:38.167 --> 00:07:39.958
I sent them the videos of Vienna,

141
00:07:40.042 --> 00:07:41.917
and they're saving
one of the slots for her.

142
00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.292
Is it free?

143
00:07:44.792 --> 00:07:46.125
How much is it?

144
00:07:47.042 --> 00:07:48.875
$75,000 a year.

145
00:07:52.417 --> 00:07:55.333
I marinated the brisket in ketchup all day
like you said Grandma used to.

146
00:07:55.417 --> 00:07:56.750
Absolutely incredible.

147
00:07:56.833 --> 00:07:57.917
You crushed it, Vivi.

148
00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.083
Vienna, you're gonna
have to make more. I'm starving.

149
00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:01.292
Easy, Bobby. Make your own.

150
00:08:01.375 --> 00:08:03.917
- Terry, how about I make you cry?
- Are you freaking kidding?

151
00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.167
Yeah! Strangle him! Use it!

152
00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.125
Put the fork down! Not the fork.

153
00:08:08.208 --> 00:08:10.500
We fight in the basement,
not at the table.

154
00:08:10.583 --> 00:08:12.000
- Sorry, Daddy.
- Sorry.

155
00:08:12.083 --> 00:08:13.250
It's all right.

156
00:08:14.167 --> 00:08:15.667
How's work going, boys?

157
00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:18.000
I gotta say, Pop,
I'm loving the road crew.

158
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.625
I'm killing it at the car wash.

159
00:08:23.542 --> 00:08:25.958
I'm going for Employee of the Month
at the drugstore.

160
00:08:26.042 --> 00:08:28.292
Whoop, whoop, whoop.

161
00:08:28.375 --> 00:08:30.333
I've been keeping the sky safe
at the airport.

162
00:08:34.917 --> 00:08:35.833
Dude!

163
00:08:35.917 --> 00:08:39.458
You guys wouldn't have to be working
if I didn't lose all our money.

164
00:08:39.542 --> 00:08:41.833
- We don't need no money.
- Money's for snobs.

165
00:08:41.917 --> 00:08:44.750
Everybody needs money
to chase their dreams.

166
00:08:45.292 --> 00:08:47.042
You guys didn't even go to college

167
00:08:47.125 --> 00:08:50.208
because you thought you had to
stick around here and keep an eye on me.

168
00:08:50.292 --> 00:08:51.583
What are you talking about?

169
00:08:51.667 --> 00:08:54.292
- …we got brisket, we got hockey here.
- …we got food.

170
00:08:54.375 --> 00:08:57.625
I'm just psyched you thought
any of us could get into college.

171
00:08:57.708 --> 00:08:59.083
He's not going to college.

172
00:08:59.167 --> 00:09:00.875
That's what he was talking about.

173
00:09:00.958 --> 00:09:02.750
It's a turn of phrase. Not saying...

174
00:09:02.833 --> 00:09:04.667
Turn of phrase? You just said...

175
00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:05.792
Say your phrase.

176
00:09:05.875 --> 00:09:06.917
It makes no sense.

177
00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.167
I know what it means.

178
00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:11.375
You turn and you look at somebody
and you say some...

179
00:09:11.458 --> 00:09:15.417
<i>Here, it's never ending
Can't remember when it started</i>

180
00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:20.542
<i>Pass around the lampshade
There'll be plenty enough room in jail</i>

181
00:09:23.875 --> 00:09:27.583
<i>If being wrong's a crime
I'm serving forever</i>

182
00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:31.125
<i>If being strong's your kind
I need help…</i>

183
00:09:31.208 --> 00:09:33.167
I'm telling you now,
I'm getting the waterbed.

184
00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:35.331
What are you talking about?
I shot tied the waterbed.

185
00:09:35.375 --> 00:09:37.458
- Enough out of you.
- What?

186
00:09:37.542 --> 00:09:39.708
You're on the floor.
You popped the waterbed.

187
00:09:39.792 --> 00:09:41.875
- Come on, let's go.
- All right.

188
00:09:41.958 --> 00:09:44.917
- Night, guys. Love you.
- Thanks for coming.

189
00:09:45.708 --> 00:09:46.792
Call me when you get there.

190
00:09:47.875 --> 00:09:49.958
Wait a minute. How are there four of you?

191
00:09:50.042 --> 00:09:54.042
Wait a minute. Who's steering?
Gordy, don't steer with your feet.

192
00:09:54.125 --> 00:09:55.750
Chips off the old block, huh?

193
00:09:55.833 --> 00:09:57.042
Hey, Uncle John Daly.

194
00:09:57.125 --> 00:09:58.250
Hey, Vienna, Happy.

195
00:09:58.333 --> 00:09:59.250
Hey, pal.

196
00:09:59.333 --> 00:10:02.333
I'm almost out of here.
I just put a down payment on a tent.

197
00:10:02.417 --> 00:10:04.500
Will you stop? I don't want you to leave.

198
00:10:04.583 --> 00:10:06.000
Stay as long as you need to.

199
00:10:06.083 --> 00:10:08.792
I appreciate you.
You want to come watch <i>Love Island?</i>

200
00:10:08.875 --> 00:10:12.000
I do, but I'm going to have
a couple of nightcaps

201
00:10:12.083 --> 00:10:13.917
and get some rest for work tomorrow.

202
00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.375
Make that scratch, dog.

203
00:10:15.458 --> 00:10:17.667
Absolutely. Good night, my brother.

204
00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.208
Night, night. Love you.

205
00:10:19.292 --> 00:10:20.292
Love you.

206
00:10:20.792 --> 00:10:22.917
Oh, my God. I hope he marries her.

207
00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:25.167
<i>She going for it.</i>

208
00:10:28.125 --> 00:10:29.958
I should be putting you to bed.

209
00:10:33.792 --> 00:10:36.875
Look, Dad, I know Miss Simon
talked to you about dance school,

210
00:10:36.958 --> 00:10:38.167
but don't even think about it.

211
00:10:38.792 --> 00:10:41.750
When I was a teenager,
I wanted to be on the Bruins.

212
00:10:41.833 --> 00:10:43.625
This is your Bruins.

213
00:10:43.708 --> 00:10:47.333
Except you know how to dance
and I didn't know how to skate.

214
00:10:47.417 --> 00:10:50.458
Did you know Mama was a great dancer?

215
00:10:50.542 --> 00:10:51.708
Yeah, she was.

216
00:10:52.292 --> 00:10:53.750
Get some sleep, Dad.

217
00:10:55.417 --> 00:10:57.917
Yeah, she was something else.

218
00:10:58.875 --> 00:11:00.167
Good night, Dad.

219
00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:02.083
Good night, Virginia.

220
00:11:11.083 --> 00:11:14.375
I can't believe that me in cheap lingerie

221
00:11:14.458 --> 00:11:18.333
carrying two pitchers of Moosehead
was your "happy place."

222
00:11:19.333 --> 00:11:20.833
I'm sorry, Virginia.

223
00:11:20.917 --> 00:11:24.250
Oh, sweetie, don't worry.
I'm not here to judge your fantasies.

224
00:11:24.333 --> 00:11:28.083
No, not that. I'm sorry about…

225
00:11:28.167 --> 00:11:29.833
Killing me with a tee shot?

226
00:11:31.208 --> 00:11:32.292
Come on.

227
00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.292
You've apologized for that
a thousand times.

228
00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.458
Look, Happy, I know you're worried
about the kids' futures,

229
00:11:40.333 --> 00:11:43.250
but you've got to show them by example.

230
00:11:44.042 --> 00:11:46.375
Let them see
the Happy I fell in love with.

231
00:11:46.458 --> 00:11:48.958
- I'm not that man anymore.
- Mmm.

232
00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.167
Okay. No, no, no.

233
00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:55.083
- Please.
- No, no.

234
00:11:55.167 --> 00:11:57.875
Can you just hold on to that
for a second, sweetie?

235
00:11:57.958 --> 00:12:02.958
Honey, you'll always be the greatest,
but you need some purpose.

236
00:12:03.833 --> 00:12:05.625
So I'm gonna tell you
what I always told you.

237
00:12:05.708 --> 00:12:06.875
Okay.

238
00:12:08.083 --> 00:12:10.083
You're not a hockey player, Happy.

239
00:12:11.417 --> 00:12:13.000
You are a...

240
00:12:56.417 --> 00:12:58.750
Hey, where you going
with those clubs, punk?

