to play in this new league?

486
00:27:09.500 --> 00:27:12.167
I've already got my golfers
and they're the best.

487
00:27:12.250 --> 00:27:13.917
You think they're better than the pros?

488
00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:16.167
I don't think, Stat. I know.

489
00:27:16.250 --> 00:27:18.208
You should think about
talking to Happy Gilmore.

490
00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:20.417
I don't know who that is.

491
00:27:21.083 --> 00:27:24.208
- Yeah, tell that to the lobsters.
- Mmm.

492
00:27:24.292 --> 00:27:26.500
Johnny, what are you doing
with those chicken wings?

493
00:27:26.583 --> 00:27:29.292
They've been in the fridge
for three weeks now, bro.

494
00:27:29.375 --> 00:27:32.542
I just put this sauce on them.
It gets rid of all the bacteria.

495
00:27:32.625 --> 00:27:35.042
Hmm. I don't know about that,
but good luck.

496
00:27:36.292 --> 00:27:38.458
When you've done that, the TV remote.

497
00:27:38.542 --> 00:27:40.833
Always wondered why that didn't work.

498
00:27:40.917 --> 00:27:42.500
What are you doing on that contuder?

499
00:27:42.583 --> 00:27:43.792
I'm looking for a job.

500
00:27:43.875 --> 00:27:47.167
There's a new Dairy Queen
around here. I think they're hiring.

501
00:27:47.250 --> 00:27:49.833
You're not going to make
$330,000 at no Dairy Queen.

502
00:27:49.917 --> 00:27:51.333
You know what you got to do.

503
00:27:51.417 --> 00:27:55.417
I tried the golf.
The golf didn't work out. Cuckoo clock.

504
00:27:55.500 --> 00:27:58.417
Grandma's cuckoo clock?
That's sacrilegious, Daddy.

505
00:27:58.500 --> 00:28:01.625
Yeah, I know.

506
00:28:01.708 --> 00:28:04.000
You can't give up
because of one bad round.

507
00:28:04.083 --> 00:28:06.125
You had to at least
hit a couple decent shots.

508
00:28:06.208 --> 00:28:09.167
I think I hit one out of 117.

509
00:28:09.250 --> 00:28:10.500
Yeah, next time you'll hit two

510
00:28:10.583 --> 00:28:13.083
and then three, and before you know it,
you're the best again.

511
00:28:13.167 --> 00:28:14.875
I'm 58 years old, V.

512
00:28:14.958 --> 00:28:16.375
Forget about being the best.

513
00:28:16.458 --> 00:28:19.125
If you finish 30th
in the Tour Championship,

514
00:28:19.208 --> 00:28:22.000
- you make 100 grand, brother.
- How am I going to finish 30th?

515
00:28:22.083 --> 00:28:24.833
I lost to three idiots
on a municipal course.

516
00:28:24.917 --> 00:28:26.167
You were hammered.

517
00:28:26.250 --> 00:28:29.083
Maybe you need to practice, Dad,
like I do with dancing.

518
00:28:29.167 --> 00:28:31.625
What else are you going to do, sober boy?
You can't drink.

519
00:28:32.458 --> 00:28:33.833
Hand sanitizer.

520
00:28:35.500 --> 00:28:36.958
Let Uncle John take care of that.

521
00:28:39.208 --> 00:28:42.542
This is hand sanitizer.

522
00:28:42.625 --> 00:28:44.000
Gotcha.

523
00:28:46.667 --> 00:28:49.458
- Were you Happy Gilmore?
- Shh.

524
00:28:50.792 --> 00:28:53.125
Um, do you want to try some clubs?

525
00:28:53.833 --> 00:28:55.167
I do, yes.

526
00:28:56.250 --> 00:28:58.792
Here, try the six iron.
A lot of pros like it.

527
00:29:02.958 --> 00:29:04.917
Yep, uh, that'll do.

528
00:29:08.250 --> 00:29:10.083
<i>He could picture the scene</i>

529
00:29:10.958 --> 00:29:12.750
<i>Put his ear to the wall</i>

530
00:29:13.458 --> 00:29:15.042
No.

531
00:29:15.958 --> 00:29:17.917
<i>He heard one guitar…</i>

532
00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:19.500
To the right… Ooh!

533
00:29:20.417 --> 00:29:21.417
Goddamn.

534
00:29:21.500 --> 00:29:22.750
Hold my blanket.

535
00:29:22.833 --> 00:29:24.292
Hold your blanket, all right.

536
00:29:25.292 --> 00:29:29.583
All right, you want to load
on the back leg…

537
00:29:29.667 --> 00:29:30.542
Uh-huh.

538
00:29:30.625 --> 00:29:32.333
- And then…
- Yeah.

539
00:29:33.417 --> 00:29:36.542
Okay, I'll… I'll handle it.
Thank you. I appreciate it.

540
00:29:36.625 --> 00:29:39.125
- I don't know what happened.
- Just do your thing.

541
00:29:39.208 --> 00:29:41.625
Go!

542
00:29:43.125 --> 00:29:44.500
You got to be quicker.

543
00:29:47.625 --> 00:29:49.167
What are you doing, Dad? Hey.

544
00:29:49.250 --> 00:29:53.542
Sobriety is a journey, not a destination.

545
00:29:54.125 --> 00:29:56.458
<i>I believe in you, Happy!</i>

546
00:29:56.542 --> 00:29:59.375
<i>Someday he's going to make it
To the top</i>

547
00:29:59.458 --> 00:30:02.833
<i>And be a juke box hero</i>

548
00:30:02.917 --> 00:30:05.458
<i>Got stars in his eyes</i>

549
00:30:05.542 --> 00:30:07.917
<i>He's a juke box hero…</i>

550
00:30:08.917 --> 00:30:12.708
"What my teacher didn't understand,
what she couldn't understand,

551
00:30:12.792 --> 00:30:14.917
"is that I only cheated on the test

552
00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:19.500
because my mother had yelled at me
about the oatmeal cookies. Yet again…"

553
00:30:25.625 --> 00:30:28.208
Oh, there he goes.

554
00:30:29.083 --> 00:30:32.042
Nice even strokes. Thank you, Charlotte.

555
00:30:33.333 --> 00:30:36.083
Good. Finish the louvers,
then do the borders.

556
00:30:36.167 --> 00:30:37.000
Yes, sir.

557
00:30:37.083 --> 00:30:39.958
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome Vienna Gilmore.

558
00:30:40.042 --> 00:30:43.417
Everyone else sucks
and you know it! Let's go, V!

559
00:30:43.500 --> 00:30:47.458
<i>Like a trip through the past
To that day in the rain</i>

560
00:30:47.542 --> 00:30:48.583
Come on, Happy!

561
00:30:48.667 --> 00:30:53.583
<i>And that one guitar
Made his whole life change</i>

562
00:30:54.292 --> 00:30:55.708
<i>Now he needs to keep on rocking</i>

563
00:30:57.417 --> 00:30:58.625
<i>He just can't stop</i>

564
00:30:59.792 --> 00:31:01.625
Happy! Happy!

565
00:31:01.708 --> 00:31:05.083
<i>That boy has got to stay on top</i>

566
00:31:08.542 --> 00:31:13.292
Happy! Happy! Happy!

567
00:31:13.375 --> 00:31:16.958
<i>He's got stars in his eyes</i>

568
00:31:17.042 --> 00:31:20.417
<i>-Juke box hero
-Got stars in his eyes</i>

569
00:31:20.500 --> 00:31:22.625
Boot!

570
00:31:22.708 --> 00:31:25.250
Come on, baby! You're back! Let's go.

571
00:31:39.625 --> 00:31:41.917
Do you mind?

572
00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:42.833
I'm sorry.

573
00:31:42.917 --> 00:31:44.458
What the hell are you doing?

574
00:31:44.542 --> 00:31:46.375
I'll take off. Have a good day.

575
00:31:46.458 --> 00:31:49.375
Go back to your mobile home.

576
00:31:49.458 --> 00:31:51.250
Got you a little something, Pop.

577
00:31:51.333 --> 00:31:54.000
What? What is it?

578
00:31:54.083 --> 00:31:56.167
"Thirty days sober! Congrats, Daddy!"

579
00:31:59.167 --> 00:32:02.250
You paint my house, brother.

580
00:32:06.958 --> 00:32:09.292
Get him on the ground!

581
00:32:17.833 --> 00:32:19.583
We'll put a little extra into this one.

582
00:32:19.667 --> 00:32:22.125
Happy! Happy! Happy!

583
00:32:24.667 --> 00:32:27.625
I am so sorry. I did not mean to do that.

584
00:32:29.083 --> 00:32:31.917
<i>Juke box hero</i>

585
00:32:33.333 --> 00:32:35.667
<i>Juke box hero</i>

586
00:32:39.417 --> 00:32:42.875
Damn you, Happy Gilmore!

587
00:32:45.667 --> 00:32:48.750
I put a thermos of coffee in your
passenger seat, Dad, and a protein bar.

588
00:32:48.833 --> 00:32:50.292
I love that. Thank you, Vivi.

589
00:32:50.375 --> 00:32:52.125
You gonna bring back another gold jacket?

590
00:32:52.208 --> 00:32:54.042
Don't be disappointed
if that doesn't happen.

591
00:32:54.125 --> 00:32:55.708
Just looking to get in the top 30.

592
00:32:55.792 --> 00:32:58.250
But that gets you enough money
to send Vienna to dance school.

593
00:32:58.333 --> 00:33:00.875
You gotta do it.
One of us kids has to amount to something.

594
00:33:00.958 --> 00:33:03.625
What are you talking about?
You're all something.

595
00:33:03.708 --> 00:33:07.250
Something to me.
Get in here. Love you guys.

596
00:33:07.333 --> 00:33:10.833
This is the first time you're gonna be
far away from us since Mom left.

597
00:33:10.917 --> 00:33:13.333
We can FaceTime Dad every day.
It'll be okay.

598
00:33:13.417 --> 00:33:15.625
- Yeah, day or night. You hear me?
- Yeah.

599
00:33:15.708 --> 00:33:18.833
And I'll be back Sunday to see you goons.
I promise you.

600
00:33:18.917 --> 00:33:20.833
Hopefully with one of them big checks.

601
00:33:20.917 --> 00:33:23.167
Hell yeah, Dad. Let's go.

602
00:33:23.250 --> 00:33:25.000
Make sure John Daly
doesn't sleep in my bed.

603
00:33:25.083 --> 00:33:26.458
If he does, no M&M's. Okay?

604
00:33:26.542 --> 00:33:27.542
- Got it.
- Got it.

605
00:33:31.917 --> 00:33:33.292
Arnold.

606
00:33:34.208 --> 00:33:35.458
Jack-o.

607
00:33:36.792 --> 00:33:37.833
Tiger.

608
00:33:39.417 --> 00:33:40.417
SpongeBob?

609
00:33:41.292 --> 00:33:42.583
What is that?

610
00:33:42.667 --> 00:33:44.792
What's with the beaver teeth?

611
00:33:44.875 --> 00:33:46.542
The truth can hurt sometimes.

612
00:33:46.625 --> 00:33:50.042
- Oh, my goodness. Dougie boy!
- Happy!

613
00:33:50.125 --> 00:33:53.792
I missed you, bro.
How's everything been going?

614
00:33:53.875 --> 00:33:56.125
Oh, it gets harder every year, Happy.

615
00:33:56.208 --> 00:33:58.375
How's it getting harder? I'm not around.

616
00:33:58.458 --> 00:34:00.750
Yeah, honestly, the Maxi Golf League.

617
00:34:00.833 --> 00:34:03.750
The Maxi… I saw a commercial for that.
It looked stupid.

618
00:34:03.833 --> 00:34:07.208
- Well, supposedly, it is faster-paced…
- Yeah, yeah.

619
00:34:07.292 --> 00:34:10.500
…and our biggest sponsors
are suddenly slow to call me back.

620
00:34:10.583 --> 00:34:12.500
I got a bad feeling about this.

621
00:34:12.583 --> 00:34:16.500
We got the greatest golfers in the world.
That's what people want to see, the best.

622
00:34:16.583 --> 00:34:18.542
Manatee says his guys are better.

623
00:34:18.625 --> 00:34:20.333
There's only one way to find out.

624
00:34:20.417 --> 00:34:22.542
Challenge him.
People would love to watch that.

625
00:34:22.625 --> 00:34:26.042
Wow! Virginia really rubbed off on you.

626
00:34:26.125 --> 00:34:27.458
We had five kids together.

627
00:34:27.542 --> 00:34:29.000
She rubbed off on me all the time,

628
00:34:29.083 --> 00:34:31.333
and I just laid there
like a sack of potatoes.

629
00:34:31.417 --> 00:34:34.708
As charming as ever. Hey, just get inside.

630
00:34:34.792 --> 00:34:36.417
The guys are excited to see you.

631
00:34:36.500 --> 00:34:40.583
Would you at least get Invisalign
for that thing? Thank you.

632
00:34:41.500 --> 00:34:44.583
Hey, Happy, you gonna finish off
that blueberry jubilee?

633
00:34:44.667 --> 00:34:48.458
Oh, God. Freddy's still snaking
everybody's dessert? Okay, you got it.

634
00:34:48.542 --> 00:34:49.958
Thank you. Cheers.

635
00:34:50.042 --> 00:34:52.750
I'm so happy to be with you.
Look forward to getting out there.

636
00:34:52.833 --> 00:34:54.500
You gonna play tomorrow?

637
00:34:54.583 --> 00:34:56.042
Why, you guys aren't playing?

638
00:34:56.125 --> 00:34:58.292
Happy, these kids are 20, 30 years old.

639
00:34:58.375 --> 00:34:59.500
We're old and stiff.

640
00:34:59.583 --> 00:35:01.333
We're old, but we're still cool.

641
00:35:01.417 --> 00:35:04.083
You guys taking aspirin
before you get out there?

642
00:35:04.167 --> 00:35:05.792
I'm popping them like Tic Tacs.

643
00:35:05.875 --> 00:35:08.083
I grind them in my applesauce.

644
00:35:08.167 --> 00:35:10.583
I used to be able to play 72 holes
without breaking a sweat.

645
00:35:10.667 --> 00:35:12.833
Now it takes me ten minutes
to get out of this chair.

646
00:35:12.917 --> 00:35:14.833
Yes?

647
00:35:14.917 --> 00:35:17.458
Do you mind grabbing me
a half iced tea and half lemonade?

648
00:35:17.542 --> 00:35:18.833
Arnold Palmer.

649
00:35:18.917 --> 00:35:21.792
No, Jack Nicklaus,
but I do get that a lot.

650
00:35:22.500 --> 00:35:24.083
Fantastic. Be back in a jiff.

651
00:35:24.750 --> 00:35:28.083
Happy, what gives with the comeback
attempt after all these years?

652
00:35:28.167 --> 00:35:29.458
Well, I'm out of cash.

653
00:35:29.542 --> 00:35:34.417
My daughter has an opportunity
to go to this ballet school in Paris, so…

654
00:35:34.500 --> 00:35:36.792
Happy, I've known you for 30 years.

655
00:35:36.875 --> 00:35:39.000
You're like a son to me.
How much you need?

656
00:35:39.083 --> 00:35:40.250
300 grand.

657
00:35:40.333 --> 00:35:42.458
Good luck tomorrow. Hit 'em straight.

658
00:35:43.167 --> 00:35:44.708
- Excuse me, pal?
- Yes, sir?

659
00:35:44.792 --> 00:35:48.250
I asked for a Tanqueray and tonic,
but they gave me Bombay instead.

660
00:35:48.333 --> 00:35:52.042
I'm the busboy, sir.
Sorry. I will get you a server right now.

661
00:35:52.125 --> 00:35:54.458
Uh, do you want some bread?

662
00:35:54.542 --> 00:35:56.500
No, just the right booze, thanks.

663
00:35:56.583 --> 00:35:57.875
Okay.

664
00:35:57.958 --> 00:35:59.208
I think I rattled him.

665
00:35:59.292 --> 00:36:03.042
Hey, Happy, whatever happened to that guy,
uh, Shooter McGavin?

666
00:36:03.125 --> 00:36:05.458
I believe he's still
in an institution, Jack.

667
00:36:05.542 --> 00:36:06.708
Wasn't he friends with O.J.?

668
00:36:06.792 --> 00:36:09.875
Well, they used to vacation together.
I don't know if they were friends, but…

669
00:36:16.917 --> 00:36:18.792
This guy's losing it.

670
00:36:25.792 --> 00:36:28.375
What are you doing here? It's quiet time.

671
00:36:28.458 --> 00:36:31.083
You suddenly got some
very powerful friends, McGavin.

672
00:36:31.708 --> 00:36:35.042
This is a court order
for your immediate release.

673
00:36:35.750 --> 00:36:39.167
Excuse me?
Gentleman would like new gin and tonic.

674
00:36:39.250 --> 00:36:42.458
He said Bombay, no Tanqueray.

675
00:36:42.542 --> 00:36:44.625
You told Spiethy that was on me, man?

676
00:36:44.708 --> 00:36:45.833
No, no.

677
00:36:45.917 --> 00:36:48.625
You threw me under the bus.
So you could be the hero?

678
00:36:48.708 --> 00:36:49.625
No. I… No.

679
00:36:49.708 --> 00:36:52.500
You stabbed me in my back.
That's what time it is?

680
00:36:52.583 --> 00:36:53.708
He just, he just said…

681
00:36:53.792 --> 00:36:57.167
I can't work like this, man.
Watching my six all day, every day.

682
00:36:57.250 --> 00:36:59.292
I just wanted to help. I offered bread.

683
00:36:59.375 --> 00:37:00.875
You mess around, you find out.

684
00:37:01.833 --> 00:37:02.833
You're fired.

685
00:37:02.875 --> 00:37:03.875
Fired?

686
00:37:08.042 --> 00:37:11.000
Hey, pal. Yo. You think
you were a little harsh on the dude?

687
00:37:11.083 --> 00:37:13.083
Sorry you had to hear that, Mr. Gilmore.

688
00:37:14.042 --> 00:37:17.625
You don't know the back story.
Mr. Couples? More blueberry jubilee?

689
00:37:17.708 --> 00:37:20.292
Nah, I'm okay. Maybe one more.

690
00:37:20.375 --> 00:37:22.333
Yeah. Back in two.

691
00:37:25.667 --> 00:37:27.792
Yackety-yack, don't come back.

692
00:37:29.667 --> 00:37:30.667
Whoo!

693
00:37:31.917 --> 00:37:33.250
Ah!

694
00:37:39.792 --> 00:37:44.792
Shooter McGavin. I'm such a massive fan.

695
00:37:45.917 --> 00:37:50.500
Gentlemen, thank you for being here
at the Tour Champions Dinner.

696
00:37:51.458 --> 00:37:52.583
That's what she said.

697
00:37:55.750 --> 00:37:57.042
I'm not sure that made sense, X.

698
00:37:57.125 --> 00:38:01.750
Every time our sport has overcome
a challenge, we have come out stronger.

699
00:38:01.833 --> 00:38:04.833
Today's challenge is the Maxi Golf League,

700
00:38:04.917 --> 00:38:08.458
who allege that they are
going to make golf more watchable.

701
00:38:08.542 --> 00:38:09.792
That's what she said.

702
00:38:12.458 --> 00:38:14.625
- Great joke, Mr. Schauffele.
- Thanks, buddy.

703
00:38:14.708 --> 00:38:16.833
I just got off the phone
with the president

704
00:38:16.917 --> 00:38:19.417
of this new league, Frank Manatee,

705
00:38:19.500 --> 00:38:22.000
and I challenged him to a competition.

706
00:38:22.083 --> 00:38:26.542
Frank accepted that challenge
and then farted into the phone.

707
00:38:27.292 --> 00:38:28.292
He did what?

708
00:38:29.083 --> 00:38:30.417
What's the competition?

709
00:38:30.500 --> 00:38:33.417
Our five best players
versus his five best.

710
00:38:33.500 --> 00:38:37.167
Make it our five worst. It doesn't matter.
We're gonna smoke them anyway!

711
00:38:39.667 --> 00:38:41.833
- Whoo!
- Yeah!

712
00:38:41.917 --> 00:38:46.083
Now, I know that you all want the honor
of kicking their ass.

713
00:38:46.167 --> 00:38:47.792
- Yeah!
- So how about this?

714
00:38:47.875 --> 00:38:51.792
Top five finishers this weekend
represent us in the challenge.

715
00:38:51.875 --> 00:38:53.583
All right. Let's go.

716
00:38:54.625 --> 00:38:56.375
That's what she said.

717
00:38:57.125 --> 00:39:00.125
Gentlemen, by showing
the world our dominance,

718
00:39:00.208 --> 00:39:04.583
we will eliminate this league
before it even officially launches.

719
00:39:04.667 --> 00:39:06.750
Let's go!

720
00:39:09.667 --> 00:39:12.292
And now you've got something else
to play for, Happy.

721
00:39:14.208 --> 00:39:17.667
Yeah! Yeah!

722
00:39:19.458 --> 00:39:23.458
Gosh. I think there's a fork in my ass.

723
00:39:23.542 --> 00:39:25.083
Now that's what she said.

724
00:39:26.417 --> 00:39:28.708
Yeah!

725
00:39:36.083 --> 00:39:38.625
<i>The sun is shining.
The greens are shimmering.</i>

726
00:39:38.708 --> 00:39:40.583
<i>What a day to play some golf.</i>

727
00:39:40.667 --> 00:39:44.917
<i>Welcome to the big one,
the U.S. Bank Tour Championship.</i>

728
00:39:45.000 --> 00:39:48.625
I'm Verne Lundquist.
Here, as always, with Jack Beard.

729
00:39:48.708 --> 00:39:52.417
And the golfer everyone is talking about,
Happy Gilmore.

730
00:39:52.500 --> 00:39:53.625
- Looks handsome.
- Yeah.

731
00:39:53.708 --> 00:39:57.250
<i>Gilmore returns after a ten-year absence.</i>

732
00:39:57.333 --> 00:39:59.083
<i>Some of the guys set your locker up.</i>

733
00:40:01.292 --> 00:40:05.333
Bengay, Tums. Preparation H, yeah.

734
00:40:05.417 --> 00:40:06.833
MiraLAX, always good.

735
00:40:06.917 --> 00:40:10.750
And, uh, diapers. Now that's pushing it.

736
00:40:16.458 --> 00:40:18.292
I know you never made it
to the Bruins, Happy,

737
00:40:18.375 --> 00:40:20.375
but maybe you'll make
this five-man wrecking crew.

738
00:40:20.458 --> 00:40:25.208
Oh, I doubt that, Tony. I'm actually
just worried about making the cut.

739
00:40:25.292 --> 00:40:26.792
Mr. Gilmore, Sergio told me

740
00:40:26.875 --> 00:40:30.417
you forgot to bring a caddie
to your first tournament. Is that true?

741
00:40:30.500 --> 00:40:32.417
He said that? No.

742
00:40:32.500 --> 00:40:35.708
Well, yeah, but still,
I didn't know the rules back then.

743
00:40:35.792 --> 00:40:37.167
That's insane.

744
00:40:37.250 --> 00:40:40.625
Yeah, that was silly.
Can't believe I would do that.

745
00:40:48.250 --> 00:40:52.417
Hey, brother. Good to see you, man.
So here's what happened.

746
00:40:52.500 --> 00:40:56.250
My regular caddie moved to Switzerland
for tax purposes,

747
00:40:56.333 --> 00:40:58.583
so I'm kind of like, I got nowhere to go.

748
00:40:58.667 --> 00:41:01.500
What do you say,
you and me for old times' sake?

749
00:41:01.583 --> 00:41:03.250
That's nice, Mr. Gilmore,

750
00:41:03.333 --> 00:41:06.500
but I, unfortunately,
I can't caddie for you today.

751
00:41:06.583 --> 00:41:10.042
You're not still mad about
the whole choking you thing, are you?

752
00:41:10.125 --> 00:41:11.625
No, it's not that.

753
00:41:11.708 --> 00:41:14.042
It's actually, I don't caddie anymore.

754
00:41:14.125 --> 00:41:17.292
I, uh… I play now.
We're actually playing together today.

755
00:41:17.375 --> 00:41:20.833
I didn't know that, Blondie.
All right, well, I'll see you out there.

756
00:41:20.917 --> 00:41:21.917
I'll see ya.

757
00:41:23.292 --> 00:41:24.792
Blondie.

758
00:41:25.417 --> 00:41:30.000
My name's Will, and I'm still mad at you
for choking me out, you son of a bitch.

759
00:41:30.083 --> 00:41:32.708
<i>We're minutes away from the start,</i>

760
00:41:32.792 --> 00:41:37.375
<i>and Happy Gilmore is apparently
breaking in yet another new caddie.</i>

761
00:41:37.458 --> 00:41:39.167
Uh, it's a club. Yeah.

762
00:41:39.250 --> 00:41:41.250
Club. Oh, like the club sandwich.

763
00:41:41.333 --> 00:41:42.833
Not the club sandwich. Okay.

764
00:41:42.917 --> 00:41:45.417
<i>Let's check in with our own Gary Potter,</i>

765
00:41:45.500 --> 00:41:48.333
who's with number one-ranked
Scottie Scheffler.

766
00:41:48.417 --> 00:41:49.333
<i>Thanks, Verne.</i>

767
00:41:49.417 --> 00:41:51.417
<i>Scottie, you have been on quite a tear.</i>

768
00:41:51.500 --> 00:41:53.667
<i>My God.
You're seeing the ball and the hole,</i>

769
00:41:53.750 --> 00:41:56.667
<i>and the position of the ball
and the hole… all good things.</i>

770
00:41:56.750 --> 00:41:58.708
<i>Is there a question in there, Gary?</i>

771
00:41:58.792 --> 00:42:02.167
<i>Scottie, if you're the best,
does that make everyone else the worst?</i>

772
00:42:03.125 --> 00:42:04.458
<i>I'm just gonna go warm up.</i>

773
00:42:04.542 --> 00:42:07.958
<i>Always great catching up with Scottie.
Back to you, Verne.</i>

774
00:42:08.042 --> 00:42:09.500
Thanks, Gary.

775
00:42:10.583 --> 00:42:14.833
The threesome of Justin Thomas,
Will Zalatoris,

776
00:42:14.917 --> 00:42:18.417
<i>and Happy Gilmore is about to tee off.</i>

777
00:42:20.917 --> 00:42:23.417
Ooh.

778
00:42:26.083 --> 00:42:27.917
Nice. Nice bang, JT.

779
00:42:28.000 --> 00:42:29.708
Pressure's on with Happy watching.

780
00:42:29.792 --> 00:42:31.125
My family loves you.

781
00:42:31.208 --> 00:42:33.167
I'm actually rooting for you.
I gotta stop.

782
00:42:33.250 --> 00:42:35.708
No. Keep it coming.
I need all the love I can get.

783
00:42:35.792 --> 00:42:36.625
Gotcha.

784
00:42:36.708 --> 00:42:38.958
Now on the tee, Zalatoris, Will.

785
00:42:40.833 --> 00:42:43.083
That's your name?

786
00:42:43.667 --> 00:42:46.083
"That's your name?" What an idiot.

787
00:42:46.167 --> 00:42:50.000
I'm a little intimidated.
All these guys hit it big now, you know?

788
00:42:50.083 --> 00:42:52.500
Do you need a water refill?
Any bread sticks?

789
00:42:52.583 --> 00:42:55.667
No. Maybe I'll go to my happy place.

790
00:42:56.792 --> 00:42:58.417
Okay. I will be here.

791
00:43:05.042 --> 00:43:07.542
It's not working.
I don't drink beer anymore.

792
00:43:08.625 --> 00:43:09.792
Good.

793
00:43:09.875 --> 00:43:12.750
Now on the tee, Gilmore, Happy.

794
00:43:12.833 --> 00:43:14.500
Welcome back, Happy!

795
00:43:14.583 --> 00:43:18.750
<i>Golf fans around the world
are excited to see Happy Gilmore again,</i>

796
00:43:18.833 --> 00:43:20.542
<i>but at 58 years old,</i>

797
00:43:20.625 --> 00:43:25.375
<i>I'm not sure even Gilmore thinks
he can compete with today's best.</i>

798
00:43:25.458 --> 00:43:26.333
Hey, Happy!

799
00:43:26.417 --> 00:43:28.417
I guess I need to update my happy place

800
00:43:28.500 --> 00:43:31.750
to something a little more
age appropriate.

801
00:43:33.875 --> 00:43:36.458
Whoa!

802
00:43:48.208 --> 00:43:51.167
You can do it!

803
00:44:01.042 --> 00:44:02.708
Yeah.

804
00:44:27.583 --> 00:44:28.708
Okay.

805
00:44:29.375 --> 00:44:31.792
<i>Thank you, Happy!</i>

806
00:44:31.875 --> 00:44:34.500
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

807
00:44:35.458 --> 00:44:37.583
Never did that before. Thank you, man.

808
00:44:37.667 --> 00:44:40.333
Okay, well, let's get...
All right, we're going to go.

809
00:44:40.417 --> 00:44:42.833
- But you bring those. Those always come.
- Oh.

810
00:44:43.625 --> 00:44:45.625
All right? That's it, that's it.

811
00:44:45.708 --> 00:44:46.583
I'm sorry.

812
00:44:46.667 --> 00:44:49.333
No, no. They got a strap
if you want to use the strap.

813
00:45:01.917 --> 00:45:05.333
A snake! Get it off me, god damn it!

814
00:45:05.417 --> 00:45:07.042
Get the snake!

815
00:45:09.000 --> 00:45:10.917
Come on. Come on. Come on.

816
00:45:11.583 --> 00:45:15.750
Goal! Yeah, baby!

817
00:45:18.625 --> 00:45:21.000
Come on, Happy!

818
00:45:21.083 --> 00:45:22.667
<i>Man, I don't drink.</i>

819
00:45:23.667 --> 00:45:25.000
How about some coffee?

820
00:45:25.083 --> 00:45:28.250
That I can do! Let's go.
Let's go. Let's go.

821
00:45:28.333 --> 00:45:31.458
Chug, chug, chug!

822
00:45:33.583 --> 00:45:36.042
Yeah!

823
00:45:37.542 --> 00:45:40.542
Yeah! Let's go! Yeah!

824
00:45:47.125 --> 00:45:49.583
Holy shit!

825
00:46:02.667 --> 00:46:04.250
Still the man, Happy!

826
00:46:04.333 --> 00:46:06.583
It's my kids. Sorry, everyone.

827
00:46:06.667 --> 00:46:08.625
<i>- Good to see you, boy!</i>
- There they are.

828
00:46:08.708 --> 00:46:11.208
Daddy's on the tee…
Wanna see Daddy drive the ball?

829
00:46:11.292 --> 00:46:14.333
Please, dear. Thank you.
All right, boys. This is for you.

830
00:46:17.792 --> 00:46:19.125
Whoa!

831
00:46:19.208 --> 00:46:21.917
Oh! Daddy got a hold of that one.

832
00:46:22.958 --> 00:46:24.292
What are you doing?

833
00:46:24.375 --> 00:46:27.458
Gordy! You got to see a doctor about that!

834
00:46:27.542 --> 00:46:28.583
Happy! Happy! Happy!

835
00:46:28.667 --> 00:46:31.667
<i>Entering day two
and feeding off the fans' support,</i>

836
00:46:31.750 --> 00:46:34.917
<i>Happy Gilmore has jumped into the top ten.</i>

837
00:46:35.000 --> 00:46:37.792
Oscar. Where were you? Who's this?

838
00:46:37.875 --> 00:46:40.000
Oh, he's Esteban, my caddie.

839
00:46:40.083 --> 00:46:41.000
- Okay.
- Steven.

840
00:46:41.083 --> 00:46:42.208
Steven, nice to meet…

841
00:46:42.292 --> 00:46:44.875
No. You don't get a caddie.
Caddies don't get caddies. I'm sorry.

842
00:46:44.958 --> 00:46:46.333
No? Can he play?

843
00:46:46.417 --> 00:46:47.875
What do you mean… He's not…

844
00:46:47.958 --> 00:46:50.583
This is the pro tournament.
I'm sorry. He's gotta go.

845
00:46:55.042 --> 00:46:57.917
Happy Gilmore! Okay, got it. Okay.

846
00:46:58.000 --> 00:46:59.833
All right. Ciao. <i>Adiós.</i>

847
00:46:59.917 --> 00:47:01.500
He took his hat.

848
00:47:01.583 --> 00:47:03.500
All right, go!

849
00:47:03.583 --> 00:47:07.083
Okay, we got to play, man.
Let me have the driver.

850
00:47:13.875 --> 00:47:17.500
Oh, damn it.

851
00:47:17.583 --> 00:47:20.292
Wait! Please!

852
00:47:21.000 --> 00:47:22.333
Now he gets it.

853
00:47:28.875 --> 00:47:30.268
- Happy! Happy!
- That was the shot.

854
00:47:30.292 --> 00:47:32.875
Daddy! Daddy! Daddy!

855
00:47:32.958 --> 00:47:35.625
<i>And heading into Saturday, two shots back.</i>

856
00:47:35.708 --> 00:47:38.125
<i>The comeback kid, Happy Gilmore.</i>

857
00:47:38.208 --> 00:47:41.792
Good shot, Happy!

858
00:47:51.667 --> 00:47:54.792
Happy! Rules!

859
00:47:54.875 --> 00:47:57.083
Happy! Happy!

860
00:47:58.292 --> 00:48:01.583
Guys, what are you doing?
I'm trying to watch your dad play golf!

861
00:48:01.667 --> 00:48:04.417
- Guys, we can't hear!
- Come on, guys.

862
00:48:04.500 --> 00:48:06.792
<i>No one could have expected this.</i>

863
00:48:06.875 --> 00:48:08.458
<i>Happy Gilmore.</i>

864
00:48:08.542 --> 00:48:12.042
From off the couch to the top
of the leader board.

865
00:48:12.125 --> 00:48:14.833
<i>And what was supposed to be
a nostalgic footnote</i>

866
00:48:14.917 --> 00:48:19.000
<i>has turned into one of the best
three rounds anyone has ever seen.</i>

867
00:48:19.083 --> 00:48:22.292
The thing is,
if I go for this and miss the cup,

868
00:48:22.375 --> 00:48:25.125
it's going to roll
right off the green, so… yeah.

869
00:48:25.208 --> 00:48:27.000
- Okay, I see.
- Yeah.

870
00:48:27.083 --> 00:48:28.375
What's a green?

871
00:48:28.458 --> 00:48:31.083
Green? Know what?
Don't worry about that right now.

872
00:48:31.167 --> 00:48:34.167
What I'm looking for
is some positive energy, you know?

873
00:48:34.250 --> 00:48:35.125
Can I help?

874
00:48:35.208 --> 00:48:38.083
Actually, you can.
Remember the happy place I went to?

875
00:48:38.167 --> 00:48:40.208
- Yes.
- You go to yours.

876
00:48:40.958 --> 00:48:42.375
Okay, I'll try.

877
00:48:48.542 --> 00:48:49.542
What's up, man?

878
00:48:50.042 --> 00:48:52.125
What do you got there? Honey?

879
00:48:53.292 --> 00:48:57.417
What is this? What is this?

880
00:48:57.500 --> 00:48:59.750
Is this about the job? Come on...

881
00:49:00.500 --> 00:49:04.417
Let's... That's... Come on, man.

882
00:49:06.250 --> 00:49:10.583
Oh, no. Not a bear. Not a bear.

883
00:49:10.667 --> 00:49:12.958
Goddamn you, busboy!

884
00:49:20.708 --> 00:49:23.167
- I'm happy now. Hit the ball.
- Yeah.

885
00:49:23.250 --> 00:49:24.542
Yes.

886
00:49:24.625 --> 00:49:27.750
You were thinking about
a bear eating that waiter, weren't you?

887
00:49:27.833 --> 00:49:28.708
Yes.

888
00:49:28.792 --> 00:49:32.333
- I thought so. Was there honey involved?
<i>- Un poquito.</i>

889
00:49:32.417 --> 00:49:33.958
I love it.

890
00:49:34.042 --> 00:49:35.208
Come on, Happy.

891
00:49:36.208 --> 00:49:39.667
Come on, Happy.

892
00:49:40.625 --> 00:49:43.167
<i>Oh, no. I don't see that one stopping.</i>

893
00:49:43.250 --> 00:49:44.833
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

894
00:49:44.917 --> 00:49:47.917
<i>Zalatoris' ball marker to the rescue!</i>

895
00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:49.792
Yeah, Blondie!

896
00:49:49.875 --> 00:49:52.042
<i>And the fairy tale continues.</i>

897
00:49:52.125 --> 00:49:55.750
<i>Happy Gilmore has somehow
turned back the hands of time.</i>

898
00:49:58.375 --> 00:50:00.583
- No. Not again.
- Come here. Come on!

899
00:50:01.875 --> 00:50:03.792
We gotta do it!

900
00:50:03.875 --> 00:50:06.750
Oh!

901
00:50:06.833 --> 00:50:11.000
I love it! Yeah, Oscar! Whoo!

902
00:50:11.083 --> 00:50:13.375
<i>Less than two months
after hitting rock bottom</i>

903
00:50:13.458 --> 00:50:15.250
<i>in a drunken golf cart crash,</i>

904
00:50:15.333 --> 00:50:20.250
<i>Happy Gilmore is 18 holes away
from a seventh gold jacket.</i>

905
00:50:20.333 --> 00:50:22.167
The only possible conclusion is that

906
00:50:22.250 --> 00:50:25.875
Happy Gilmore has reached an agreement
of some kind

907
00:50:25.958 --> 00:50:29.375
with Satan, a.k.a. the Devil!

908
00:50:29.458 --> 00:50:32.208
All right. Let's go! Happy!

909
00:50:32.292 --> 00:50:33.792
- Good job, Mr. Gilmore.
- What's up?

910
00:50:33.875 --> 00:50:35.042
In the zone today. Man.

911
00:50:35.125 --> 00:50:37.875
We were putting. We were doing okay.
A little luck involved.

912
00:50:37.958 --> 00:50:39.792
Hey, Mr. Gilmore. Billy Jenkins.

913
00:50:39.875 --> 00:50:41.792
- Hey, nice to meet you, Bobby.
- Billy.

914
00:50:41.875 --> 00:50:44.583
Billy was on fire today.
I was like, where did that come from?

915
00:50:44.667 --> 00:50:47.208
Had the best round of my life.
I'm in second place.

916
00:50:47.292 --> 00:50:48.667
You and me play tomorrow.

917
00:50:48.750 --> 00:50:50.250
You're kidding. Look forward to that.

918
00:50:50.333 --> 00:50:53.083
I've never been in the hunt.
It's a dream come true.

919
00:50:53.167 --> 00:50:55.125
You're going to love it.
You get in the top five,

920
00:50:55.208 --> 00:50:57.833
you get to play against those buffoons
from the new league.

921
00:50:57.917 --> 00:50:59.792
What's up with that tool
starting that league?

922
00:50:59.875 --> 00:51:01.500
The guy came to see me to talk about it.

923
00:51:01.583 --> 00:51:04.417
He had the worst breath
I've ever smelled in my life.

924
00:51:04.500 --> 00:51:05.833
Like somebody died in his mouth

925
00:51:05.917 --> 00:51:08.042
or a donkey took a shit there
or something…

926
00:51:08.125 --> 00:51:10.167
It was not good.
Anyways, I got to get to a meeting.

927
00:51:10.250 --> 00:51:12.500
Love you, Bubba. David, good to see you.

928
00:51:12.583 --> 00:51:13.833
It's Billy.

929
00:51:13.917 --> 00:51:19.208
So, in summary, I am no
longer allowed to purchase magic markers

930
00:51:19.292 --> 00:51:20.792
in the state of Connecticut.

931
00:51:20.875 --> 00:51:23.750
I am Nate, and I am one day sober.

932
00:51:26.917 --> 00:51:30.208
Nate, you're an example to us all.

933
00:51:30.833 --> 00:51:31.667
What?

934
00:51:31.750 --> 00:51:33.667
Before we finish,
I'd like to say a few words

935
00:51:33.750 --> 00:51:36.167
about the remarkable achievement
of our brother, Happy.

936
00:51:36.250 --> 00:51:39.375
We've been watching you play, Mr. Gilmore.
So inspiring.

937
00:51:39.458 --> 00:51:44.750
Yeah! Happy Gilmore, making Black people
like golf again.

938
00:51:44.833 --> 00:51:46.208
That's right, Bessie.

939
00:51:46.292 --> 00:51:49.375
I just hope Happy's able to
continue to play as well tomorrow.

940
00:51:50.083 --> 00:51:52.792
Tomorrow being of course… Oh…

941
00:51:54.083 --> 00:51:55.292
Mother's Day.

942
00:51:58.708 --> 00:52:02.292
<i>Welcome to the final round
of the Tour Championship.</i>

943
00:52:02.375 --> 00:52:04.042
<i>Here come your current leaders.</i>

944
00:52:04.125 --> 00:52:05.458
<i>Journeyman Billy Jenkins,</i>

945
00:52:05.542 --> 00:52:10.000
<i>getting his first taste of success
after an undistinguished career.</i>

946
00:52:10.083 --> 00:52:11.667
<i>The only man in his way,</i>

947
00:52:11.750 --> 00:52:16.625
<i>a golf magician
named Happy Octavius Gilmore.</i>

948
00:52:16.708 --> 00:52:18.833
Octavius is his middle name?

949
00:52:18.917 --> 00:52:21.167
Nah, but it sounds cool, doesn't it?

950
00:52:21.917 --> 00:52:22.917
Wait a minute.

951
00:52:23.750 --> 00:52:27.042
Can't wear shorts, Mr. Jenkins.
It's a two-stroke penalty.

952
00:52:27.125 --> 00:52:28.625
That's okay.

953
00:52:28.708 --> 00:52:31.958
I don't want to be hot today.
Makes my balls itchy.

954
00:52:32.833 --> 00:52:35.667
<i>Was that confidence
or just pure stupidity?</i>

955
00:52:42.167 --> 00:52:45.500
Now on the tee, Gilmore, Happy.

956
00:52:45.583 --> 00:52:47.083
Nice shot, young man.

957
00:52:48.333 --> 00:52:51.333
<i>Happy Gilmore will try to defend
his eight-shot lead</i>

958
00:52:51.417 --> 00:52:53.625
<i>on this glorious Mother's Day.</i>

959
00:53:07.250 --> 00:53:10.667
<i>Gilmore was aiming right for some reason,
and that's where it went.</i>

960
00:53:11.458 --> 00:53:12.875
A lot of holes left to play.

961
00:53:12.958 --> 00:53:13.958
Yeah.

962
00:53:14.708 --> 00:53:18.083
It's okay.

963
00:53:21.958 --> 00:53:24.125
Mr. McGavin.

964
00:53:24.208 --> 00:53:25.375
How'd you sleep?

965
00:53:25.458 --> 00:53:28.292
This place… is amazing.

966
00:53:28.375 --> 00:53:29.875
The pillows, the steam shower,

967
00:53:29.958 --> 00:53:31.083
the free porn,

968
00:53:31.167 --> 00:53:33.917
and these fluffy pancakes. Oh, my God.

969
00:53:34.000 --> 00:53:35.917
What do you say you and I go on a tour

970
00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:38.542
- and I show you what we're all about?
- Mmm…

971
00:53:38.625 --> 00:53:41.417
I'll make sure there's a fresh stack
waiting for you when we get back.

972
00:53:41.500 --> 00:53:42.625
All right.

973
00:53:44.208 --> 00:53:45.583
Slippers on?

974
00:53:45.667 --> 00:53:48.125
And why don't you throw on
some underpants, too?

975
00:53:48.208 --> 00:53:49.708
It's all right, Happy.

976
00:53:49.792 --> 00:53:51.542
Hey, Happy. Remember me?

977
00:53:53.042 --> 00:53:55.708
My dad used to be your boss
when you worked in construction.

978
00:53:55.792 --> 00:53:57.458
I'm truly proud of you.

979
00:53:57.542 --> 00:54:00.125
Hey, thanks a lot, Mr. Larson.

980
00:54:00.750 --> 00:54:04.125
Drago Larson. Little Drago Larson?

981
00:54:04.208 --> 00:54:06.500
Hell yeah! My God!

982
00:54:06.583 --> 00:54:10.042
I always felt bad about what I did
to Daddy and the whole nail thing.

983
00:54:10.125 --> 00:54:11.583
Actually, after he got it removed,

984
00:54:11.667 --> 00:54:13.875
he kind of missed it,
so he had it put back.

985
00:54:13.958 --> 00:54:15.542
Oh, okay.

986
00:54:15.625 --> 00:54:17.500
He passed away a few years ago.

987
00:54:17.583 --> 00:54:19.333
I'm so sorry. What happened?

988
00:54:19.417 --> 00:54:21.208
He rolled over in his sleep.

989
00:54:21.292 --> 00:54:22.417
Oh, yeah.

990
00:54:22.500 --> 00:54:25.833
At least I still have Mom.
Every boy needs his mom.

991
00:54:26.542 --> 00:54:28.917
- Yeah.
- Happy have five kids, Mom.

992
00:54:29.000 --> 00:54:31.417
Oh, tell your wife Happy Mother's Day.

993
00:54:32.417 --> 00:54:34.000
His wife passed away.

994
00:54:34.708 --> 00:54:37.292
Oh, I'm so sorry, sweetheart.

995
00:54:37.375 --> 00:54:39.500
Why didn't you tell me, Jerko?

996
00:54:39.583 --> 00:54:41.792
Mommy, don't hit me. Mommy, don't hit me.

997
00:54:41.875 --> 00:54:43.458
Which club do you prefer, sir?

998
00:54:43.542 --> 00:54:44.667
Let's go, Gilmore!

999
00:54:44.750 --> 00:54:48.542
Give me… Let me have a wedge.

1000
00:54:51.875 --> 00:54:53.167
Let's go, Happy.

1001
00:54:54.042 --> 00:54:56.708
- Every boy needs a mom.
- But we don't have one.

1002
00:54:56.792 --> 00:54:58.125
You got it, Happy.

1003
00:54:58.208 --> 00:54:59.667
- You can make it.
- You got this.

1004
00:54:59.750 --> 00:55:01.208
Do it. Come on.

1005
00:55:04.500 --> 00:55:08.417
Oh!

1006
00:55:09.292 --> 00:55:10.792
I gotta go to the bathroom.

1007
00:55:13.875 --> 00:55:16.000
You came at a very special moment.

1008
00:55:16.083 --> 00:55:17.208
Change is in the air.

1009
00:55:17.292 --> 00:55:18.542
What change is that?

1010
00:55:18.625 --> 00:55:21.000
Golf. New and improved.

1011
00:55:22.417 --> 00:55:24.375
Gilmore must love all this.

1012
00:55:24.458 --> 00:55:26.875
I wouldn't know.
Happy Gilmore's a broken man.

1013
00:55:27.583 --> 00:55:28.625
A broken man?

1014
00:55:28.708 --> 00:55:31.042
Yeah, ever since the loss of his wife.

1015
00:55:31.125 --> 00:55:33.250
Wait, Virginia Venit?

1016
00:55:33.333 --> 00:55:34.625
Is that what her name was?

1017
00:55:35.375 --> 00:55:36.375
Oh, man.

1018
00:55:38.583 --> 00:55:40.292
<i>Fart recognized.</i>

1019
00:55:42.458 --> 00:55:43.958
All right, come on in.

1020
00:55:44.042 --> 00:55:46.167
<i>Our current leader, Happy Gilmore,</i>

1021
00:55:46.250 --> 00:55:49.417
<i>has been in the restroom
for an unusually long time.</i>

1022
00:56:32.208 --> 00:56:33.875
Let's play some golf.

1023
00:56:36.042 --> 00:56:39.208
<i>Billy Jenkins is playing
an inspired round.</i>

1024
00:56:40.458 --> 00:56:44.167
Meanwhile, Happy Gilmore is struggling
to keep it in the fairway.

1025
00:56:47.667 --> 00:56:49.250
Cart path.

1026
00:56:51.750 --> 00:56:53.583
Wanna sip of my 3-wood?

1027
00:56:53.667 --> 00:56:55.542
- No, <i>gracias.</i>
- Okay.

1028
00:56:59.792 --> 00:57:01.417
You scratch it, I hurt you.

1029
00:57:04.292 --> 00:57:06.125
Thank you, Jesus!

1030
00:57:06.833 --> 00:57:08.125
<i>Plenty golf to be played.</i>

1031
00:57:08.208 --> 00:57:10.333
Happy, what does Mother's Day mean to you?

1032
00:57:10.417 --> 00:57:13.750
Can you suck my white ass, Gary?
Just suck the entire thing?

1033
00:57:16.417 --> 00:57:17.417
<i>Psycho.</i>

1034
00:57:23.375 --> 00:57:24.458
Oh.

1035
00:57:24.542 --> 00:57:28.333
<i>And it has all fallen apart
for Happy Gilmore…</i>

1036
00:57:28.417 --> 00:57:32.250
Happy's… wasted!

1037
00:57:32.333 --> 00:57:35.875
…who is staggering,
literally, to the finish.

1038
00:57:37.833 --> 00:57:41.708
What I'm about to show you
is the foundation of Maxi Golf.

1039
00:57:44.917 --> 00:57:47.167
An X-ray from 1957.

1040
00:57:47.917 --> 00:57:49.000
Who's Ben Daggett?

1041
00:57:49.083 --> 00:57:53.542
He's the only guy who could hit it farther
than Happy Octavius Gilmore.

1042
00:57:54.792 --> 00:57:56.417
<i>How come I never heard of him?</i>

1043
00:57:56.500 --> 00:57:58.792
<i>Well, he was a degenerate.
Couldn't putt for shit.</i>

1044
00:57:58.875 --> 00:58:01.375
<i>Just drove around the country
in the 1950s,</i>

1045
00:58:01.458 --> 00:58:03.583
<i>dominating long drive contests.</i>

1046
00:58:03.667 --> 00:58:06.708
<i>They say he could
carry the ball 500 yards.</i>

1047
00:58:06.792 --> 00:58:10.000
<i>One day, one of the mobsters
who he owed some money to</i>

1048
00:58:10.083 --> 00:58:12.500
<i>took a golf shoe
and shoved it right up Ben's ass.</i>

1049
00:58:13.333 --> 00:58:15.667
<i>And that's where this X-ray was taken.</i>

1050
00:58:18.042 --> 00:58:20.250
Do you see anything unusual here?

1051
00:58:20.333 --> 00:58:23.958
Well, there appears to be a shoe
up his rectal region.

1052
00:58:24.042 --> 00:58:26.250
That's true. But see that?

1053
00:58:26.333 --> 00:58:29.750
That's the iliolumbar ligament.
Why is it in two pieces?

1054
00:58:29.833 --> 00:58:32.208
Let me guess. Shoe up the ass?

1055
00:58:32.292 --> 00:58:33.708
- No.
- No?

1056
00:58:33.792 --> 00:58:35.750
This happened much earlier in his life.

1057
00:58:35.833 --> 00:58:39.000
Turns out Daggett severed it
in a childhood go-kart accident.

1058
00:58:39.083 --> 00:58:41.792
<i>The separation of the ligament
from when he was a kid</i>

1059
00:58:41.875 --> 00:58:44.625
<i>increased Daggett's range of motion
in his hips,</i>

1060
00:58:44.708 --> 00:58:46.833
<i>dramatically improving
the amount of torque</i>

1061
00:58:46.917 --> 00:58:49.125
<i>and club speed that he could generate.</i>

1062
00:58:51.500 --> 00:58:53.708
That's why he could hit it so far.
Because of the shoe.

1063
00:58:53.792 --> 00:58:56.292
Will you stop with the shoe?
We're done with the shoe.

1064
00:58:56.375 --> 00:58:59.458
It was a go-kart accident
that severed the ligament

1065
00:58:59.542 --> 00:59:01.792
and turned him into
a long-ball-hitting freak.

1066
00:59:02.333 --> 00:59:04.292
And all those golfers outside?

1067
00:59:04.375 --> 00:59:06.958
We snipped
their iliolumbar ligaments, too.

1068
00:59:07.042 --> 00:59:10.083
That's cheating.
Who would agree to a surgery like that?

1069
00:59:10.792 --> 00:59:13.417
<i>Journeymen…
who were good enough for the pros</i>

1070
00:59:13.500 --> 00:59:15.667
<i>but could never figure out
how to beat the legends.</i>

1071
00:59:23.792 --> 00:59:27.792
It's all in the hips, Grandpa.
It's all in the hips.

1072
00:59:29.667 --> 00:59:32.083
Shooter, I want you to be the captain
of the Maxi team.

1073
00:59:32.167 --> 00:59:33.375
Hmm.

1074
00:59:33.458 --> 00:59:35.917
- Thank you so much.
- Absolutely, Mr. Manatee.

1075
00:59:36.000 --> 00:59:37.833
Pancakes next time.

1076
00:59:37.917 --> 00:59:40.292
And I haven't even showed you
the best part yet.

1077
00:59:43.625 --> 00:59:46.167
18 holes? Boring.

1078
00:59:46.250 --> 00:59:47.625
We do seven holes.

1079
00:59:48.208 --> 00:59:50.917
Slow play? We got shot clocks.

1080
00:59:51.000 --> 00:59:53.125
My God, this is obscene.

1081
00:59:53.208 --> 00:59:55.208
It's a lot to take in. I get it.

1082
00:59:55.292 --> 00:59:58.000
I will never have anything
to do with this…

1083
00:59:59.250 --> 01:00:01.042
This abomination.

1084
01:00:01.125 --> 01:00:04.042
You know, Shooter, it wasn't very easy
to get you released.

1085
01:00:04.833 --> 01:00:07.667
But it'd be pretty damn easy
to get you recommitted.

1086
01:00:07.750 --> 01:00:09.000
Yeah?

1087
01:00:09.083 --> 01:00:11.375
Damn, that's hot.

1088
01:00:11.458 --> 01:00:13.417
- I was told you liked it hot.
- Do you?

1089
01:00:27.542 --> 01:00:30.417
My eye!

1090
01:00:32.833 --> 01:00:36.750
<i>Yesterday, Happy Gilmore had
the entire sports world rooting for him,</i>

1091
01:00:36.833 --> 01:00:40.292
<i>and then he took all that good will
and basically set it on fire.</i>

1092
01:00:40.375 --> 01:00:42.625
<i>- Go to your happy place!
- No!</i>

1093
01:00:42.708 --> 01:00:45.542
<i>He also lost out on playing
against the Maxi League</i>

1094
01:00:45.625 --> 01:00:48.083
<i>as he finds himself
with a sixth-place finish.</i>

1095
01:00:48.167 --> 01:00:50.875
And so it is Jenkins
who will lead the five-man team

1096
01:00:50.958 --> 01:00:55.458
against the upstart Maxi League,
or… so we thought.

1097
01:00:55.542 --> 01:00:57.500
Sorry to pee in your punch bowl, folks,

1098
01:00:57.583 --> 01:01:01.917
but I am actually a proud member
of the Maxi Golf League.

1099
01:01:02.000 --> 01:01:04.625
Bye-bye, regular golf. Bye-bye.

1100
01:01:04.708 --> 01:01:06.667
That's right. Billy's part of a new league

1101
01:01:06.750 --> 01:01:09.500
where we hit longer,
look cooler, and party harder.

1102
01:01:09.583 --> 01:01:12.000
And the best part is,
our guys are "Maxi Good."

1103
01:01:12.083 --> 01:01:13.375
Give me the jacket.

1104
01:01:13.458 --> 01:01:15.542
<i>My sources in the DA's office say</i>

1105
01:01:15.625 --> 01:01:17.375
Gilmore's actions
violated a plea agreement,

1106
01:01:17.458 --> 01:01:20.583
relating to his drunken golf cart crash
earlier this year,

1107
01:01:20.667 --> 01:01:24.125
and that he only avoided arrests
due to an ally causing a distraction.

1108
01:01:26.625 --> 01:01:29.750
Hey, Drago,
you forgot your underpants, Jerko!

1109
01:01:29.833 --> 01:01:32.625
Gilmore is now facing six years
in state prison,

1110
01:01:32.708 --> 01:01:35.917
but I hope the authorities
will deliver justice to golf fans

1111
01:01:36.000 --> 01:01:42.125
by sentencing him to the electric chair,
which at this point, he richly deserves.

1112
01:01:57.125 --> 01:02:00.250
Oh, Virginia,
I'm sorry you're no longer with us.

1113
01:02:00.333 --> 01:02:02.625
You were a woman
working in a man's league.

1114
01:02:02.708 --> 01:02:05.375
I bet that wasn't easy. Huh?

1115
01:02:06.167 --> 01:02:11.292
Yeah. I guess I should also apologize
for asking you to get me a Pepsi.

1116
01:02:11.375 --> 01:02:12.375
Diet.

1117
01:02:16.333 --> 01:02:17.375
Gilmore.

1118
01:02:18.125 --> 01:02:19.875
Shooter McGavin.

1119
01:02:19.958 --> 01:02:25.792
Last time I saw you, you were running away
in slow motion with my gold jacket.

1120
01:02:25.875 --> 01:02:27.292
That was my jacket!

1121
01:02:27.375 --> 01:02:30.625
Take it. I've got five others.

1122
01:02:33.583 --> 01:02:36.042
God! You would never
have won them if I wasn't...

1123
01:02:36.125 --> 01:02:38.250
What? In the loony bin?

1124
01:02:38.917 --> 01:02:40.750
You stole my life from me.

1125
01:02:40.833 --> 01:02:44.500
Now, why would I want
to steal the life of somebody

1126
01:02:45.417 --> 01:02:48.333
who eats pieces of shit…

1127
01:02:48.417 --> 01:02:51.167
- Oh, you…
- …for breakfast?

1128
01:02:59.375 --> 01:03:02.333
Game over, bitch.

1129
01:03:04.625 --> 01:03:05.625
- Come on.
- Okay.

1130
01:03:05.708 --> 01:03:07.583
- Let's go.
- We're gonna fist fight?

1131
01:03:07.667 --> 01:03:08.667
- Want this?
- Yeah.

1132
01:03:08.750 --> 01:03:10.958
You sure you want that? Come on.

1133
01:03:18.625 --> 01:03:19.625
Come here, now.

1134
01:03:20.708 --> 01:03:22.417
That was for you, Grandma.

1135
01:03:22.500 --> 01:03:24.583
I am so sorry I lost the house again.

1136
01:03:24.667 --> 01:03:25.917
- Truly.
- Hi, Grandma.

1137
01:03:26.000 --> 01:03:28.458
Don't you ever talk to my grandma!

1138
01:03:28.542 --> 01:03:29.750
Come on.

1139
01:03:31.125 --> 01:03:33.083
Jackass!

1140
01:03:44.583 --> 01:03:46.042
That was round one.

1141
01:03:46.125 --> 01:03:49.417
We are done, son.
You can tell everybody you won.

1142
01:03:50.500 --> 01:03:53.667
Should I put my hair in a bun
just for fun?

1143
01:03:53.750 --> 01:03:56.792
And play one-on-one with Attila the Hun?

1144
01:03:56.875 --> 01:03:59.625
Oh, boy. That was good. Round two.

1145
01:04:00.208 --> 01:04:01.833
Okay. We're even.

1146
01:04:01.917 --> 01:04:03.542
Come on. You love this.

1147
01:04:04.417 --> 01:04:06.833
- Get up. Absolutely.
- Thanks, man.

1148
01:04:06.917 --> 01:04:10.375
Okay. Hey.
Are your hip ligaments cut in half?

1149
01:04:11.458 --> 01:04:12.458
I don't think so.

1150
01:04:12.542 --> 01:04:14.917
Anyone ever stick a shoe up your ass?

1151
01:04:15.000 --> 01:04:16.667
Not that I can recollect.

1152
01:04:16.750 --> 01:04:18.875
You realize these are strange questions?

1153
01:04:18.958 --> 01:04:22.250
Apparently, if a certain hip ligament
is not attached,

1154
01:04:22.333 --> 01:04:23.792
you can hit the ball farther.

1155
01:04:23.875 --> 01:04:28.208
Oh. No. I always powered my drives
the old-fashioned way. With rage.

1156
01:04:28.292 --> 01:04:29.417
Yeah.

1157
01:04:29.500 --> 01:04:31.792
You want to get out of these pajamas?
I live around here.

1158
01:04:31.875 --> 01:04:32.917
Yeah, thanks.

1159
01:04:33.542 --> 01:04:39.042
<i>Mister! Mister! Get me outta here!</i>

1160
01:04:45.042 --> 01:04:47.417
They issued a warrant
for your arrest, Dad.

1161
01:04:47.500 --> 01:04:49.333
Yeah, hide in the basement.

1162
01:04:49.417 --> 01:04:51.458
I should just turn myself in.
Get it over with.

1163
01:04:51.542 --> 01:04:54.542
- We'll ask the lawyer when he gets here.
- You hired a lawyer?

1164
01:04:54.625 --> 01:04:56.750
Okay. How do I look?

1165
01:04:57.250 --> 01:04:59.292
You look like my frickin' dad.

1166
01:04:59.375 --> 01:05:00.417
Yeah.

1167
01:05:00.500 --> 01:05:03.083
At least I'm not wearing
that ridiculous Bruins jersey.

1168
01:05:03.167 --> 01:05:04.167
Uh-oh.

1169
01:05:06.500 --> 01:05:07.625
Okay.

1170
01:05:09.458 --> 01:05:10.458
Okay, get the door.

1171
01:05:14.542 --> 01:05:18.458
Mr. Gilmore. Mr. McGavin. John Daly.

1172
01:05:18.542 --> 01:05:20.667
Nice to see you again.

1173
01:05:20.750 --> 01:05:23.375
You're the lawyer?
I thought you were the IRS guy.

1174
01:05:23.458 --> 01:05:26.417
I was, but I got tired
of everybody hating me

1175
01:05:26.500 --> 01:05:28.708
and occasionally being thrown
through a glass door.

1176
01:05:28.792 --> 01:05:29.958
You hate me, don't you?

1177
01:05:34.083 --> 01:05:36.125
- Right.
- So, I went to law school.

1178
01:05:36.917 --> 01:05:40.250
You didn't want to be hated anymore,
so you became a lawyer?

1179
01:05:41.417 --> 01:05:43.375
- That's funny.
- Lawyers are snobs.

1180
01:05:43.458 --> 01:05:44.875
- Pieces of shit.
- Pieces of shit.

1181
01:05:45.708 --> 01:05:47.583
Let's sit. Lots to talk about.

1182
01:05:47.667 --> 01:05:49.917
<i>Let me just have a little shower…</i>

1183
01:05:50.583 --> 01:05:52.417
This girl's got some body on her.

1184
01:05:52.500 --> 01:05:56.333
Hey, we do not objectify women anymore.

1185
01:05:57.625 --> 01:05:58.625
What?

1186
01:05:58.667 --> 01:06:03.333
Okay, great. Uh, looks like the DA
has withdrawn the arrest warrant.

1187
01:06:03.417 --> 01:06:04.292
What?

1188
01:06:04.375 --> 01:06:06.625
Even though you appeared to some onlookers

1189
01:06:06.708 --> 01:06:08.458
to be inebriated at the tournament,

1190
01:06:08.542 --> 01:06:10.208
you weren't administered an alcohol test.

1191
01:06:10.292 --> 01:06:12.208
- And… I have better news.
- Yes?

1192
01:06:12.292 --> 01:06:14.208
You came in sixth at that tournament.

1193
01:06:14.292 --> 01:06:17.167
That's right. I forgot about that.
How much did I win?

1194
01:06:17.250 --> 01:06:18.917
Uh, $496,000.

1195
01:06:19.000 --> 01:06:20.292
- Oh, my God!
- No way!

1196
01:06:20.375 --> 01:06:21.917
- No! What?
- Holy shit!

1197
01:06:23.000 --> 01:06:24.083
Baby! Yay!

1198
01:06:24.167 --> 01:06:25.833
Now you're really gonna hate me.

1199
01:06:25.917 --> 01:06:31.042
The tour is fining you
$500,000 for bad behavior.

1200
01:06:31.125 --> 01:06:33.958
So he lost $37,000?

1201
01:06:34.042 --> 01:06:35.542
No. It's $33,000, Dad.

1202
01:06:35.625 --> 01:06:39.042
It's $4,000, you buffoons.
How is that good news?

1203
01:06:39.125 --> 01:06:42.333
Well, you came in sixth,
but the winner, Billy Jenkins,

1204
01:06:42.417 --> 01:06:45.833
opted out of the tour team
because he's playing for the bad guys.

1205
01:06:45.917 --> 01:06:47.208
So you made the team.

1206
01:06:47.292 --> 01:06:49.292
- Dad, that's great!
- Whoa! Okay, Pop.

1207
01:06:49.375 --> 01:06:51.625
They don't want me. I'm a disgrace.

1208
01:06:51.708 --> 01:06:53.292
A freaking embarrassment.

1209
01:06:53.375 --> 01:06:55.250
Let's go outside, Dad, for a second.

1210
01:06:56.000 --> 01:06:57.000
Next.

1211
01:07:00.625 --> 01:07:04.375
Well, Shooter,
due to Mr. Manatee's sworn statement,

1212
01:07:04.458 --> 01:07:08.583
you are now technically an escapee
from a mental institution.

1213
01:07:08.667 --> 01:07:11.125
Welcome to the club.

1214
01:07:12.917 --> 01:07:15.917
Dad, it doesn't matter
if you play for that team or not.

1215
01:07:16.000 --> 01:07:17.375
You have to stop drinking.

1216
01:07:17.458 --> 01:07:18.542
I did. It's just...

1217
01:07:18.625 --> 01:07:21.250
Just nothing.
You gotta find peace somehow.

1218
01:07:21.333 --> 01:07:23.333
There's no peace. I…

1219
01:07:23.417 --> 01:07:25.167
The reason I joined that tour again

1220
01:07:25.250 --> 01:07:28.208
was to get you the future you deserve,
and I lost $4,000.

1221
01:07:28.292 --> 01:07:31.042
You think if you made that money
I could leave you like this?

1222
01:07:31.125 --> 01:07:33.542
It's not your job to take care of me.
I told you.

1223
01:07:33.625 --> 01:07:36.292
- Of course it is. We're family.
- You're stuck with us.

1224
01:07:36.375 --> 01:07:37.500
Yeah, come on, Dad.

1225
01:07:37.583 --> 01:07:39.542
I don't want you to be stuck with me.

1226
01:07:39.625 --> 01:07:41.167
You didn't do nothing wrong. It's me.

1227
01:07:41.917 --> 01:07:43.792
I think this person could help.

1228
01:07:47.792 --> 01:07:50.958
Hey, you gotta put
a little mustard on that ball

1229
01:07:51.042 --> 01:07:55.292
so it doesn't get stuck
where the pirate hide his, uh, uh…

1230
01:07:55.375 --> 01:07:56.583
Booty and shit.

1231
01:07:56.667 --> 01:07:58.167
The hold?

1232
01:07:58.250 --> 01:08:00.958
Yeah, the hold. Get at it, kiddies.

1233
01:08:01.042 --> 01:08:03.625
- Thank you!
- Are you Slim Peterson?

1234
01:08:03.708 --> 01:08:05.250
That's what they call me.

1235
01:08:05.333 --> 01:08:08.333
Your dad Chubbs was my teacher.
My name's Happy Gilmore...

1236
01:08:08.417 --> 01:08:09.708
I know who you are.

1237
01:08:09.792 --> 01:08:15.375
Hey, you gotta hit it under the octopus
and bank it off one of his leg things.

1238
01:08:15.458 --> 01:08:16.458
The tentacles?

1239
01:08:16.542 --> 01:08:18.708
Yeah, testicles. Now, what was you saying?

1240
01:08:18.792 --> 01:08:21.000
I need to talk to you for a few minutes.

1241
01:08:21.083 --> 01:08:23.667
Damn, mosquitoes. They everywhere.

1242
01:08:23.750 --> 01:08:25.083
- What…
- Look at them.

1243
01:08:26.625 --> 01:08:27.708
Alligator?

1244
01:08:27.792 --> 01:08:30.208
No, vending machine.
I didn't have enough change.

1245
01:08:30.292 --> 01:08:33.167
Had to reach up there to get
my Famous Amos chocolate chip cookies.

1246
01:08:33.750 --> 01:08:37.333
Man, looking at you just reminded me
of what I did to you.

1247
01:08:37.417 --> 01:08:38.583
What'd you do to me?

1248
01:08:38.667 --> 01:08:41.208
What I did to my own kids. Stole a parent.

1249
01:08:41.292 --> 01:08:43.375
Man, you gotta forgive yourself for that.

1250
01:08:43.458 --> 01:08:44.583
Don't want to.

1251
01:08:44.667 --> 01:08:46.500
I didn't want to forgive you either,

1252
01:08:46.583 --> 01:08:48.708
because it was easier to hate you

1253
01:08:48.792 --> 01:08:51.917
than to deal with the fact
that my daddy wasn't coming back.

1254
01:08:52.583 --> 01:08:56.208
It's kind of like I was using hate
to keep him alive.

1255
01:08:56.292 --> 01:08:59.542
But once I forgave you,
I became myself again.

1256
01:08:59.625 --> 01:09:02.458
And that's who I knew
my daddy wanted me to be.

1257
01:09:05.417 --> 01:09:09.375
You loved your wife. You loved my dad.

1258
01:09:09.458 --> 01:09:11.375
And they loved you, period.

1259
01:09:11.458 --> 01:09:14.250
You know what else they loved? Golf.

1260
01:09:14.333 --> 01:09:15.792
Oh, my God, yeah.

1261
01:09:15.875 --> 01:09:17.458
I talked to your little girl,

1262
01:09:17.542 --> 01:09:20.292
and she said you got a chance
to save the whole sport

1263
01:09:20.375 --> 01:09:22.875
by playing against some clown league?

1264
01:09:22.958 --> 01:09:26.208
Yeah, well, why don't you go kick
some bozo ass then?

1265
01:09:26.292 --> 01:09:27.667
Let's do it for them.

1266
01:09:30.208 --> 01:09:32.000
I am so sorry.

1267
01:09:32.083 --> 01:09:34.250
Boy, why you had to squeeze it like that?

1268
01:09:34.333 --> 01:09:36.167
I will throw these out. I can…

1269
01:09:36.250 --> 01:09:38.250
Give them here. I got some Gorilla Glue.

1270
01:09:38.333 --> 01:09:39.750
Yeah, love you, buddy.

1271
01:09:39.833 --> 01:09:41.708
Yeah, man, thank you for stopping by.

1272
01:09:43.583 --> 01:09:46.250
You know, we could use some help.

1273
01:09:46.333 --> 01:09:50.958
Oh, about time somebody
recognized my genius. Say less.

1274
01:09:51.042 --> 01:09:52.250
Okay, okay.

1275
01:09:52.333 --> 01:09:53.958
Where do you think you're going, Slim?

1276
01:09:54.042 --> 01:09:56.042
I'm going to help save golf, Charley.

1277
01:09:56.125 --> 01:10:00.042
If you leave now, you ain't ever
coming back, you big pork chop.

1278
01:10:00.125 --> 01:10:04.125
Damn straight I ain't never coming back,
you fine-ass English hillbilly.

1279
01:10:04.875 --> 01:10:06.208
Welcome, gentlemen.

1280
01:10:06.292 --> 01:10:09.625
You are the five golfers
who will represent our tour

1281
01:10:09.708 --> 01:10:12.542
in the grudge match
against the Maxi League.

1282
01:10:13.125 --> 01:10:16.375
I don't have to tell you
how important it is that we beat them.

1283
01:10:16.458 --> 01:10:20.667
And here to talk about how we're going to
accomplish that is Shooter McGavin.

1284
01:10:22.083 --> 01:10:24.083
Thank you, Doug. I'll take it from here.

1285
01:10:25.292 --> 01:10:27.167
I want to talk to you about pressure.

1286
01:10:27.958 --> 01:10:31.333
Now, as the most successful golfer
of the '90s,

1287
01:10:31.958 --> 01:10:34.667
I've faced my share, believe me,

1288
01:10:34.750 --> 01:10:37.625
but nothing like my 30 years in the can.

1289
01:10:37.708 --> 01:10:41.125
And if I let my guard down there
for a nanosecond…

1290
01:10:41.833 --> 01:10:43.000
Stab!

1291
01:10:43.542 --> 01:10:46.167
I got a shiv in my guts.

1292
01:10:46.917 --> 01:10:49.833
Anyway, I hear you guys
all have ice water in your veins.

1293
01:10:49.917 --> 01:10:53.542
Well, I reviewed the footage
and I ain't seeing it.

1294
01:10:53.625 --> 01:10:55.792
- Man, what's happening right now?
- Uh…

1295
01:10:55.875 --> 01:10:57.000
Bryson DeChambeau.

1296
01:10:58.125 --> 01:11:01.125
2022 Portland Open. Eighth hole.

1297
01:11:01.208 --> 01:11:02.833
You got a two-stroke lead.

1298
01:11:02.917 --> 01:11:06.125
You got an opportunity
to pull way ahead and…

1299
01:11:07.333 --> 01:11:08.833
- Aw!
- What?

1300
01:11:10.458 --> 01:11:11.583
Huh?

1301
01:11:12.542 --> 01:11:13.792
Oops.

1302
01:11:14.500 --> 01:11:16.875
Come on. We all miss a putt
every now and then.

1303
01:11:16.958 --> 01:11:18.750
Scottie Scheffler.

1304
01:11:19.708 --> 01:11:20.625
Oh, boy.

1305
01:11:20.708 --> 01:11:22.958
2019 Cadillac Invitational.

1306
01:11:23.042 --> 01:11:25.417
Third hole. You're tied.
Top of the leader board.

1307
01:11:25.500 --> 01:11:28.625
It's Sunday. Pressure's on. And you…

1308
01:11:32.250 --> 01:11:33.542
Hmm. Into the woods.

1309
01:11:34.292 --> 01:11:37.208
The woods, Scottie? Are you afraid to win?

1310
01:11:37.292 --> 01:11:39.333
- What about you?
- What?

1311
01:11:39.417 --> 01:11:42.750
Yeah. 1996 Tour Championship. Final round.

1312
01:11:42.833 --> 01:11:43.833
Don't do it, boys.

1313
01:11:43.875 --> 01:11:45.583
No. This isn't relevant.

1314
01:11:45.667 --> 01:11:47.500
Four-stroke lead on the back nine?

1315
01:11:47.583 --> 01:11:49.875
The guy who beat you
got hit by a Volkswagen.

1316
01:11:49.958 --> 01:11:50.958
- Jackass!
- Jackass!

1317
01:11:51.000 --> 01:11:55.375
All right! Maybe I haven't handled
the pressure perfectly myself,

1318
01:11:55.458 --> 01:11:58.375
but I have seen the surgically modified
freaks that you're playing.

1319
01:11:58.458 --> 01:12:01.583
I have seen the monstrosity
they're making you play on.

1320
01:12:01.667 --> 01:12:07.292
And if you can't take the heat,
golf, as we know it, it's finished!

1321
01:12:09.583 --> 01:12:11.167
So let's do this!

1322
01:12:11.250 --> 01:12:12.958
Come on. Let's put them in.

1323
01:12:13.042 --> 01:12:14.042
All right. On three.

1324
01:12:14.125 --> 01:12:15.875
- One, two, three… Shooter!
- Golf!

1325
01:12:21.292 --> 01:12:23.500
Time to prepare for a moving target.

1326
01:12:23.583 --> 01:12:24.875
The cups are gonna be moving?

1327
01:12:24.958 --> 01:12:27.292
Damn it, Rory.
Nothing's off-limits for these commies.

1328
01:12:27.375 --> 01:12:29.417
- Now, Oscar's cousin…
- Esteban.

1329
01:12:29.500 --> 01:12:33.625
Esteban is fast. And elusive, I'm told.

1330
01:12:33.708 --> 01:12:35.208
He's gonna start at the red flag.

1331
01:12:35.292 --> 01:12:38.708
If he makes it to the blue flag,
we haven't done our jobs.

1332
01:12:38.792 --> 01:12:40.292
He's cool with us hitting him?

1333
01:12:40.375 --> 01:12:41.458
Yeah. He's been paid.

1334
01:12:41.542 --> 01:12:44.792
What did he say?

1335
01:12:44.875 --> 01:12:46.375
You're never gonna hit him.

1336
01:12:46.458 --> 01:12:47.583
Oh, yeah? How come?

1337
01:12:47.667 --> 01:12:49.500
I'm shifty!

1338
01:12:49.583 --> 01:12:51.875
Okay, he's shifty. He is. I've seen it.

1339
01:12:53.833 --> 01:12:55.750
<i>Get your biscuits in the kitchen</i>

1340
01:12:55.833 --> 01:12:57.292
<i>I'm a sous chef on a mission</i>

1341
01:12:57.375 --> 01:12:59.375
<i>Baby, wiggle it, it's vicious</i>

1342
01:12:59.458 --> 01:13:01.500
<i>We about to break the dishes</i>

1343
01:13:01.583 --> 01:13:03.583
<i>Got the pepper with the sodium</i>

1344
01:13:03.667 --> 01:13:06.667
<i>We cookin' with petroleum
Come step up to the podium</i>

1345
01:13:06.750 --> 01:13:07.667
It's too easy!

1346
01:13:07.750 --> 01:13:08.875
<i>And cut up this linoleum</i>

1347
01:13:10.875 --> 01:13:12.125
Yeah!

1348
01:13:12.750 --> 01:13:13.750
You got me!

1349
01:13:14.333 --> 01:13:16.375
Come on, cousin. You're almost there.

1350
01:13:28.583 --> 01:13:30.625
Okay, stop! We got him. We got him.

1351
01:13:33.542 --> 01:13:34.958
I said stop! Who did that?

1352
01:13:38.083 --> 01:13:40.792
Oscar. You sicko.

1353
01:13:41.792 --> 01:13:43.632
- So I got a hockey question for you.
- Uh-huh.

1354
01:13:43.708 --> 01:13:45.542
I notice when the players fight,

1355
01:13:45.625 --> 01:13:48.625
one of the guys is always pulling
the jersey over the head of the other guy

1356
01:13:48.708 --> 01:13:50.429
- before he starts pounding on him.
- Right.

1357
01:13:50.458 --> 01:13:51.458
- Yeah.
- Is that hard?

1358
01:13:51.500 --> 01:13:54.417
- No, it's easy. You want me to show you?
- Yes, please.

1359
01:13:54.500 --> 01:13:56.542
Brother. Can I borrow you for a second?

1360
01:13:56.625 --> 01:13:58.917
Basically all you do
is pull the shirt over.

1361
01:13:59.000 --> 01:14:00.875
This traps the arms. You know?

1362
01:14:00.958 --> 01:14:02.500
- Yeah.
- Knockout. Money.

1363
01:14:02.583 --> 01:14:03.750
- You sure?
- Yeah.

1364
01:14:03.833 --> 01:14:05.333
Okay. How much?

1365
01:14:05.417 --> 01:14:06.667
Fifty.

1366
01:14:06.750 --> 01:14:09.958
Uh, I'll give you a hundred.
Here we go. You know what I mean?

1367
01:14:10.042 --> 01:14:11.083
Yeah. That was nice.

1368
01:14:11.167 --> 01:14:13.792
- Okay. Money.
- Okay. You got it, Scottie. I'm broke.

1369
01:14:13.875 --> 01:14:15.458
- Thank you.
- There you go. Okay.

1370
01:14:15.542 --> 01:14:17.167
Great job, today, by the way.

1371
01:14:17.250 --> 01:14:19.667
- Excellent. Yeah, it's fun.
- Yeah. That was easy.

1372
01:14:19.750 --> 01:14:21.250
I love my job.

1373
01:14:21.333 --> 01:14:26.000
Mini-golf-style putting is about
two things, angles and obstacles.

1374
01:14:26.083 --> 01:14:30.000
If you can read the angles,
you can avoid the obstacles.

1375
01:14:30.083 --> 01:14:32.958
Let's putt
so we can figure those angles out.

1376
01:14:34.042 --> 01:14:35.667
Yes! Scheffler!

1377
01:14:38.292 --> 01:14:40.333
Yeah, you're right.

1378
01:14:40.417 --> 01:14:44.833
One more day before we face these chumps.
This is how I used to toughen up.

1379
01:14:52.417 --> 01:14:55.250
Oh, my God, Rory!

1380
01:14:55.333 --> 01:14:57.250
Okay, Oscar, let's see your stuff.

1381
01:15:11.417 --> 01:15:15.417
<i>Sittin' down is stupid
Now let me see you move it</i>

1382
01:15:16.208 --> 01:15:19.375
Oh! Do you want bread sticks?

1383
01:15:24.125 --> 01:15:26.708
A batting cage to toughen up?

1384
01:15:26.792 --> 01:15:29.250
I love how much we're in your head.

1385
01:15:29.333 --> 01:15:31.375
Oh, I think we're in your head, Brendan.

1386
01:15:31.458 --> 01:15:34.208
Otherwise, you wouldn't be snooping around
and following us.

1387
01:15:34.292 --> 01:15:35.292
My name is Billy.

1388
01:15:35.375 --> 01:15:36.583
Hey, settle down, Barry,

1389
01:15:36.667 --> 01:15:38.875
and get off the electric Royce.
No leaning.

1390
01:15:39.583 --> 01:15:42.708
Look, Happy, I don't want to
have to humiliate you tomorrow.

1391
01:15:43.833 --> 01:15:45.833
You're in the DNA of my league.

1392
01:15:45.917 --> 01:15:48.042
The way you rebelled
against the traditions

1393
01:15:48.125 --> 01:15:50.292
and fussiness of golf, it was beautiful.

1394
01:15:50.375 --> 01:15:53.000
So I'm gonna offer you one last chance
to be a part of it, okay?

1395
01:15:53.083 --> 01:15:53.917
Hell no.

1396
01:15:54.000 --> 01:15:57.375
And you look like Freddy Krueger
worked at Starbucks. Change it.

1397
01:15:58.042 --> 01:15:59.583
I'll give you 10% of the company.

1398
01:16:01.833 --> 01:16:04.958
I can't believe I'm the one
sticking up for tradition, but…

1399
01:16:05.042 --> 01:16:08.833
My wife liked the way
golf was played, as is.

1400
01:16:08.917 --> 01:16:11.250
And she was pretty much
right about everything.

1401
01:16:11.833 --> 01:16:15.792
So sorry, boys, but tomorrow,
your dumb league is done.

1402
01:16:15.875 --> 01:16:18.792
No, tomorrow, I'm gonna finish
the revolution you started.

1403
01:16:18.875 --> 01:16:21.000
I heard what you said
about my breath to Bubba Watson.

1404
01:16:21.083 --> 01:16:23.667
I have gingivitis. It's hereditary, okay?

1405
01:16:23.750 --> 01:16:27.167
And I got it from my great-grandfather.
So I'm so sorry.

1406
01:16:27.250 --> 01:16:29.583
I'm literally smelling it from here.

1407
01:16:29.667 --> 01:16:31.375
And the wind is blowing that way.

1408
01:16:31.458 --> 01:16:34.125
Something has to change in your life.
I'm telling you.

1409
01:16:55.333 --> 01:16:56.333
Okay.

1410
01:16:57.458 --> 01:16:58.875
Come here. Bring it in.

1411
01:16:58.958 --> 01:17:01.833
I just wanted to say thank you guys
for always getting me back on track.

1412
01:17:01.917 --> 01:17:03.292
- I love you.
- Love you.

1413
01:17:03.375 --> 01:17:06.750
This ain't about Vivi going to
dance school. It's about saving golf?

1414
01:17:06.833 --> 01:17:08.250
Maybe we can do both,

1415
01:17:08.333 --> 01:17:10.375
but we will figure that out, I promise.

1416
01:17:10.458 --> 01:17:12.750
Because we're Gilmores,
and we don't know how to stop.

1417
01:17:12.833 --> 01:17:14.500
Hell yeah, Pop, let's go!

1418
01:17:14.583 --> 01:17:16.875
And don't forget to feed John Daly
three times a day.

1419
01:17:16.958 --> 01:17:17.792
- Okay.
- Got it.

1420
01:17:17.875 --> 01:17:19.417
- Love you guys.
- You heard him.

1421
01:17:19.500 --> 01:17:20.750
Let's do this for Mom.

1422
01:17:20.833 --> 01:17:22.292
- For Mom!
- For Mommy.

1423
01:17:23.042 --> 01:17:24.500
- You got this.
- That's right.

1424
01:17:25.083 --> 01:17:26.750
That's right. She deserves it.

1425
01:17:26.833 --> 01:17:29.042
Go get 'em, Dad.

1426
01:17:29.125 --> 01:17:30.125
Pop…

1427
01:17:30.958 --> 01:17:31.958
- All right.
- Yeah!

1428
01:17:32.042 --> 01:17:33.458
- What's going on?
- Let's go.

1429
01:17:33.542 --> 01:17:34.893
- Go Dad, you got this.
- Go Daddy!

1430
01:17:34.917 --> 01:17:36.583
- What's going on?
- Stupid.

1431
01:17:37.292 --> 01:17:39.542
- Damn it.
- Are you kidding me?

1432
01:17:47.083 --> 01:17:48.250
What are you doing?

1433
01:17:48.333 --> 01:17:49.500
What's with this guy?

1434
01:17:49.583 --> 01:17:51.167
What you doing hitting my dad's car?

1435
01:17:51.250 --> 01:17:53.208
This is a family affair, bro!

1436
01:17:53.292 --> 01:17:56.583
Take him down, boys! Let's go!

1437
01:17:56.667 --> 01:17:59.167
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- What's he doing?

1438
01:17:59.250 --> 01:18:00.625
Get him!

1439
01:18:00.708 --> 01:18:01.917
Chase him! That's right!

1440
01:18:02.000 --> 01:18:03.958
- Where you going?
- Get him!

1441
01:18:04.042 --> 01:18:05.458
What the hell is happening?

1442
01:18:09.083 --> 01:18:12.375
<i>Welcome to an event
unique in the annals of sport.</i>

1443
01:18:13.083 --> 01:18:16.667
<i>A one-time showdown
between golf's greatest players</i>

1444
01:18:17.250 --> 01:18:20.792
<i>and the wild upstarts
who seek to supplant them.</i>

1445
01:18:20.875 --> 01:18:22.583
Let's get it on.

1446
01:18:22.667 --> 01:18:25.500
<i>Welcome to the Maxi Tour Challenge.</i>

1447
01:18:25.583 --> 01:18:29.125
